hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4201","Al-Walid ibn Shuja' Abu Hammam narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Zufar narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from one who heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has intercourse with his wife, let him be truthful to her (satisfy her); if he precedes her, let him not hurry her."
"4202","Abu Hammam narrated to us, 'Abd al-Majid ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from one who narrated to him, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has intercourse with his wife, let him be truthful to her; then if he fulfills his need before she fulfills her need, let him not hurry her until she fulfills her need."
"4203","Muhammad ibn Bashshar al-'Abdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah our neighbor, narrating, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Mu'adh ibn Jabal: Know that whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah enters Paradise."
"4204","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Mawraq, from Anas, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; some of us fasting and some of us breaking fast. We alighted at a stop on a hot day; those of us with the most shade were the owners of cloaks; some of us shielded themselves from the sun with the hand. He said: The fasters fell and the breakers stood, pitched the structures and watered the mounts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The breakers have taken the reward today."
"4205","'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd al-'Ammi, from Abu Iyas, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every ummah has a monasticism, and the monasticism of this ummah is jihad in the path of Allah."
"4206","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Hafari Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Khalid, from Abu Na'amah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)), Abu Bakr, and Umar would not recite ""In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."""
"4207","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Jarud, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: One of my uncles made food for the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) and said: I would love for you to eat in my house and pray in it. He said: So he came to him, and in the house there was a stallion among those stallions, so he ordered a side of it to be swept and sprinkled with water, then he prayed and we prayed with him."
"4208","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Mahdi ibn Maymun, from Ghaylan, from Anas, who said: You do deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them at the time of the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) among the deadly sins."
"4209","Isma'il ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Muslim, from Anas, who said: The Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) was commissioned as a prophet on Monday, and funeral prayer was offered over him on Tuesday."
"4210","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Musa ibn Anas ibn Malik, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: You have left behind in Madinah men: you did not travel any journey, nor spend any expenditure, nor cross any valley, but they were with you in it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can they be with us while they are in Madinah? He said: The excuse has held them back."
"4211","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abu Zilal narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)), who said: A servant in Hell will call out for a thousand years: O Hanan, O Mannan. He said: So Allah will say: O Jibril, bring My servant. He said: So Jibril will go and see the people of the Fire fallen on their faces. He said: So he will return and say: O Lord, I did not see him. He said: So Allah will say: He is in such-and-such a place. He said: So he will come to him and bring him to his Lord, and Allah will say to him: O My servant, how did you find your place and your resting place? He said: So he will say: O Lord, the worst place and the worst resting place. He said: So He will say: Return My servant. And he will say: O Lord, I never hoped that You would return me after You had brought me out. So He will say: Leave My servant."
"4212","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Abu Zilal informed us, saying: I visited Anas ibn Malik, and he said to me: When did you lose your sight? He said: I was two years old, as my family told me. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings? I said: Yes. He said: Ibn Umm Maktum passed by the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) and greeted him, then went on, and the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: Allah says: For one whose two precious things I have taken, there is no reward with Me except Paradise."
"4213","Al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Zilal narrated to me, saying: Anas narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)), who said: Two men crossed a desert: one a worshipper, and the other afflicted with frivolity. The worshipper became thirsty until he fell down. His companion kept looking at him, and with him was a small water vessel containing some water. He kept looking at him as he lay fallen, and said: By Allah, if this righteous servant dies of thirst while I have water, I will never attain any good from Allah; and if I give him my water to drink, I will surely die. So he relied upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, resolved, sprinkled some of his water on him and gave him to drink from what was left. He said: So he rose and they both crossed the desert. He said: Then the one who was afflicted will be stopped on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning, and he will be ordered to the Fire, and the angels will drive him. Then he will see the worshipper and say: O so-and-so, do you not know me? He said: He will say: Who are you? He will say: I am so-and-so who preferred you over myself on the day of the desert. He said: He will say: Yes, I know you. He said: Then he will say to the angels: Stop. He said: So he will be stopped, and he will come until he stands and supplicates his Lord, saying: O Lord, You know his kindness to me, and how he preferred me over himself. O Lord, grant him to me. And He will say: He is yours. He said: And he will come and take him by the hand and admit him into Paradise. Al-Salt said: Ja'far said: I said: Did Anas narrate it to you from the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him))? He said: Yes."
"4214","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Burjumi narrated to us, from Abu al-Zilal, from Anas ibn Malik, from his mother, who said: She had a sheep, and she collected its clarified butter in a leather skin until she filled the skin, then she sent it with Rubaybah, saying: O Rubaybah, deliver this skin to the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) so he may use it as condiment. So Rubaybah went with it until she came to the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a skin of clarified butter that Umm Sulaym has sent to you. He said: Empty her skin for her. So the skin was emptied and handed back to her, and she went off with it. Then Umm Sulaym came and saw the skin full and dripping. Umm Sulaym said: O Rubaybah, did I not order you to take it to the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him))? She said: I did; if you do not believe me, go and ask the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)). So Umm Sulaym went with Rubaybah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I sent to you with her a skin containing clarified butter. He said: She did; she brought it. She said: By Him Who sent you with guidance and the religion of truth, it is full and dripping with clarified butter. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said to her: Are you amazed that Allah has fed you as you fed His Prophet? Eat and feed others. She said: So I came home and apportioned such-and-such in a bowl of ours, and left in it enough for us to use as condiment for a month or two months."
"4215","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sulaym, from Najih Abu Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) carried out stoning, and Abu Bakr and Umar did, and the command of the two of them is Sunnah."
"4216","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Najih Abu Ali, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) carried out stoning, and Abu Bakr and Umar did, and the command of the two of them is Sunnah."
"4217","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ubayd Allah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: Do not pray at the rising of the sun nor at its setting, for it rises and sets upon the horn of Satan; and pray between that as much as you wish."
"4218","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Tha'labah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: Wondrous is the believer: no decree is decreed for him but it is good for him."
"4219","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Tha'labah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) smiled, then said: I am amazed at the believer: Allah does not decree any decree for him but it is good for him."
"4220","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, Yazid al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I never prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) with a lighter prayer than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)), nor briefer while complete."
"4221","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) was not foul-mouthed nor obscene; he would say to one of us when admonishing: What is wrong with him, may his right hand be covered with dust."
"4222","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Jamilah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: I recognize the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) for me, that He bless for me my wealth and my children."
"4223","Mujahid ibn Musa al-KhuttAli narrated to us, al-Sahmi Abu Wahb narrated to us, Sulayman al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: When Allah wants good for a people, He afflicts them with trials."
"4224","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, Hilal Abu Mu'alla ibn Hilal narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Three birds were gifted to the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)), and he fed his servant one bird. When the next day came, she brought them to him, and the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said to her: Did I not forbid you to set aside anything for tomorrow? For Allah brings the provision of every tomorrow."
"4225","Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Warith, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: Four will be brought on the Day of Resurrection: the newborn, the insane, the one who died in the period between prophets, and the decrepit old man. Each of them will speak his plea. Then the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will say to a neck of the Fire: Come forth. Then He will say to them: I used to send to My servants messengers from among themselves, and I am the messenger of Myself to you: enter this. Then those for whom wretchedness was decreed will say: O Lord, where should we enter it, when it was from it that we used to flee? He said: And those for whom happiness was decreed will go forth and plunge into it hastening. He said: Then the Blessed and Exalted will say: You were more severe in denying and disobeying My messengers. So He will admit these into Paradise and these into the Fire."
"4226","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Layth, from Abd al-Warith, from Anas, who said: Abu Taybah passed by us in Ramadan, and we said: Where have you come from? He said: I cupped the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him))."
"4227","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sadusi narrated to us, saying: Akhshan al-Sadusi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) saying: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you sin until your sins fill what is between the heaven and the earth, then you seek Allah's forgiveness, He will forgive you. And by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin, then they seek Allah's forgiveness and He forgives them."
"4228","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Jarud, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: One of my uncles made food for the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) and said: I would love for him to eat in my house and pray in it. He said: So he came to him, and in the house there was a stallion among those stallions, so he ordered a side of it to be swept and sprinkled with water, then he prayed and we prayed with him."
"4229","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, al-Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: Jibril came to me with something like a white mirror in which there was a black spot. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is Friday; Allah has made it a festival for you and your community. You come before the Jews and the Christians. In it there is an hour in which no servant coincides asking Allah for good in it but He gives it to him. He said: I said: What is this black spot? He said: This is the Day of Resurrection; it will come on Friday, and we call it with us al-Mazid. He said: I said: What is the Day of al-Mazid? He said: Allah has made in Paradise a wide valley, and made in it dunes of white musk. When Friday comes, Allah will descend therein. Pulpits of gold will be placed there for the prophets, and chairs of pearl for the martyrs, and the wide-eyed houris will come down from the chambers, and they will praise Allah and glorify Him. He said: Then Allah will say: Clothe My servants, so they will be clothed; and He will say: Feed My servants, so they will be fed; and He will say: Give drink to My servants, so they will be given drink; and He will say: Perfume My servants, so they will be perfumed. Then He will say: What do you want? And they will say: Our Lord, Your pleasure. He said: He will say: I am pleased with you. Then He will command them and they will depart, and the wide-eyed houris will ascend to the chambers, which are of green emerald and red ruby."
"4230","Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Sallam informed us, Umar ibn Ma'dan and Thabit al-Bunani, both of them, narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I attended a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) in which there was neither bread nor meat."
"4231","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, al-Muthanna al-Qattan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Abu Sukayn, narrated to me, saying: I came to Anas ibn Malik and said: Inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)). So he ordered his household, and he prayed with us Zuhr and Asr, reciting to us in a low voice: he recited al-Mursalat, and al-Nazi'at, and Amma yatasa'alun, and the like of these surahs."
"4232","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: The lifespan of a fly is forty nights, and all flies are in the Fire except the bee."
"4233","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Sinan Abu Rabi'ah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) visited a Bedouin who was ill with fever, and the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: An expiation and a purification. The Bedouin said: Rather it is a fever boiling over an old man, driving him to the graves. So the Prophet ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) got up and left him."
"4234","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Sinan Abu Rabi'ah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah ((peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) said: When Allah afflicts a Muslim with an affliction in his body, He says to the angel: Write for him the righteous deeds he used to do. If He heals him, He washes him and purifies him; and if He takes his soul, He forgives him and has mercy on him."
"4235","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Rabi'ah al-Hadrami, from Anas ibn Malik: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a daughter, such-and-such, and she mentioned her beauty and loveliness, and said: I offer her to you in preference. He said: I have accepted her. She kept praising her until she mentioned that she had never suffered a headache nor complained of anything at all. He said: I have no need of your daughter."
"4236","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Sinan Abu Rabi'ah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah afflicts a servant with an affliction in his body, He says to the angel: Write down for him the righteous deeds he used to do. If He heals him, He washes him and purifies him, and if He takes his soul, He forgives him and has mercy on him."
"4237","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Rabi'ah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant, so supplicate to Allah for him. He said: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, lengthen his life, and forgive him. He said: My wealth increased until it yielded produce twice a year, my children increased until I have buried from my own loins more than a hundred, my life grew long until I have felt shy before my family, and I have longed to meet my Lord. As for the fourth, meaning forgiveness."
"4238","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulaym al-Dabbi narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: If I take the two precious things of My servant, I am not pleased with any reward for him less than Paradise. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if it is one? He said: Even if it is one."
"4239","Shayban narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulaym al-Dabbi narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) equipped an army against the polytheists, among them Abu Bakr and Umar; he put the two of them in command, and all the people. He said to them: March swiftly, for between you and the polytheists there is water; if the polytheists reach that water before you, it will distress the people and you will be overcome by severe thirst, you and your animals and your mounts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed behind with eight men, he being the ninth of them. He said to his companions: Would you like to rest a little, then catch up with the people? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So they rested, and nothing woke them but the heat of the sun. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke, and his companions awoke. He said to them: Get up and relieve yourselves. They did so, then returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Does any of you have water? A man among them said: O Messenger of Allah, a small water-skin with a little water in it. He said: Bring it. He brought it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, wiped it with his hands and invoked blessing. Then he said to his companions: Come and perform ablution. They came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to pour for them until they performed ablution. A man among them called the adhan and the iqamah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in prayer, and said to the owner of the water-skin: Take pride in your water-skin, for it will have a story. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions rode ahead of the people. He said to his companions: What do you think the people have done? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said to them: Among them are Abu Bakr and Umar, and they will guide the people. The people arrived, and the polytheists had already reached that water, so the people were distressed and suffered severe thirst, they and their mounts and animals. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is the owner of the water-skin? He said: Here he is, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Bring your water-skin. He brought it, and in it was a little water. He said to all of them: Come and drink. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to pour for them until they all drank, and they watered their animals and mounts, and filled every water-skin, each skin and large vessel. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions advanced toward the polytheists. Allah sent a wind that struck the faces of the polytheists, Allah the Blessed and Exalted sent down His help, and gave power over their backs. They killed a great number of them, took many captives, drove off abundant spoils, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people returned safe and sound."
"4240","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulaym al-Dabbi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled or went on campaign, he would take a different man of his companions behind him each day. He said: The riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Mu'adh ibn Jabal. He called him while he was riding behind him and said: O Mu'adh ibn Jabal. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know what the right of Allah upon the servants is? That they testify that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and that they worship Him without associating anything with Him. He repeated this hadith three times. Then he called out and said: O Mu'adh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know what the right of the servants upon Allah is if they do that? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of the servants upon Allah, if they do that, is that He will not punish them and will admit them into Paradise."
"4241","Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Zarbi Abu Yahya narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character."
"4242","Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Zarbi Abu Yahya narrated to us, from Anas, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he raised his head and there was an old man approaching. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not honor our elder and have mercy on our young."
"4243","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, Zarbi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: An old man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his need, but they were slow to make room for the old man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not have mercy on our young and honor our elder."
"4244","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Muslim al-Barrad, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to accept the invitation of the slave, visit the sick, and ride the donkey."
"4245","Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Isa ibn Sadaqah ibn Abbad al-Yashkuri informed me, who said: I entered with my father to visit Anas ibn Malik, and we said to him: Narrate to us a hadith by which Allah will benefit us. I heard him saying: Whoever among you is able to die without any debt upon him, let him do so, for I saw the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the funeral of a man with a debt upon him was brought, and he said: I will not pray over him until you guarantee his debt, for my prayer over him will benefit him. They did not guarantee his debt, and he did not pray over him, and he said: He is held hostage in his grave."
"4246","Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us, who said: Isa ibn Sadaqah narrated to me, who said: I heard Anas saying: Fear Allah and render trusts to those entitled to them. Abu Ya'la said: My strongest thought is that al-Mu'alla narrated it to me from Isa, but I did not find it."
"4247","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Abi Dharrah narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who lives to forty years in Islam except that Allah turns away from him three kinds of affliction: leprosy, madness, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty, Allah makes his reckoning easy for him. When he reaches sixty, Allah grants him return to Him with what He loves. When he reaches seventy, Allah loves him and the inhabitants of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, Allah accepts his good deeds and overlooks his evil deeds. When he reaches ninety, Allah forgives him his past and future sins, he is called Allah's prisoner on earth, and he intercedes for the people of his household."
"4248","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, the like of it. Abu Khaythamah said: Anas ibn Iyad said: I am Allah's prisoner in His earth."
"4249","Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal informed me, who said: Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Ja'far ibn Amr al-Damri, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah grants life to forty years in Islam, Allah averts from him kinds of affliction: leprosy, vitiligo, and the bewilderment of Satan. Whoever Allah grants life to fifty years in Islam, Allah makes his reckoning easy on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever Allah grants life to sixty years in Islam, Allah grants him return to Allah with what Allah loves. Whoever Allah grants life to seventy years in Islam, the inhabitants of heaven and the inhabitants of earth love him. Whoever Allah grants life to eighty years in Islam, Allah effaces his evil deeds and records his good deeds. Whoever Allah grants life to ninety years in Islam, Allah forgives his sins, he is Allah's prisoner on His earth, and he intercedes for the people of his household on the Day of Resurrection."
"4250","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, who said: Two men of the people of Harran, people of knowledge, and they were trustworthy in my view, narrated to me, from Zufar ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no aged person who lives long in Islam to forty years except that Allah repels from him kinds of affliction: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty, Allah lightens his reckoning. When he reaches sixty, Allah grants him return to Allah with what Allah loves. When he reaches seventy, Allah loves him and the inhabitants of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, his good deeds are recorded and his evil deeds are effaced. When he reaches ninety, Allah forgives him his past and future sins, he is Allah's prisoner on His earth, and intercession is granted for him for the people of his household."
"4251","Yahya ibn Sulaym said: Abdullah ibn Uthman also informed me, from Sa'd ibn Abi al-Hakam al-Madani, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Anas ibn Malik, with the like of the hadith of the two Harranites."
"4252","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Sinan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No charity is accepted from misappropriated spoils, and no prayer without purification."
"4253","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sa'id ibn Sinan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: He is not a believer whose neighbor is not safe from his harms."
"4254","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Shabab narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sa'id ibn Sinan, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greatness of the reward is with the greatness of the trial."
"4255","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Shabab narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sa'id ibn Sinan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He hastens his punishment in this world, and when Allah intends evil for a servant, He withholds him for his sin until He brings him to account on the Day of Resurrection."
"4256","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid, from Ibn Sinan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: And he mentioned the like of it."
"4257","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid, from Ibn Sinan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Deliberation is from Allah, haste is from Satan. There is nothing with more excuses than Allah, and there is nothing dearer to Allah than praise."
"4258","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid, from Ibn Sinan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Guarantee for me six things and I will guarantee Paradise for you. They said: What are they? He said: When one of you speaks, let him not lie; when he promises, let him not break it; when he is trusted, let him not betray; lower your gaze, restrain your hands, and guard your private parts."
"4259","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Sinan Sa'd al-Kindi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah does not place His mercy except upon a merciful one. They said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us show mercy. He said: It is not the mercy of one of you to his companion; it is mercy to all people."
"4260","Abu Ali al-Hasan, a companion of ours, narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Sinan, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men who revile each other: what they say is upon the one who started, until the wronged one transgresses."
"4261","Abu Ali al-Hasan narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, from Sa'd ibn Sinan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who used to say: Before the Hour there will be trials like pieces of the dark night. A man will wake as a believer and enter the evening as a disbeliever, and wake as a disbeliever and enter the evening as a believer, and people will sell their religion for a small portion of this world."
"4262","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Mijlaz, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month in the dawn prayer after bowing, supplicating against Ri'l and Dhakwan."
"4263","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Mijlaz, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"4264","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Mijlaz, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"4265","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, supplicating against Ri'l and Dhakwan."
"4266","Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Basri narrated to us in Balhujaym, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rewards of my community were shown to me, even the speck of dirt a man removes from the mosque, and the sins of my community were shown to me, and I did not see a sin greater than a verse or a chapter a man learns and then forgets."
"4267","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abi Hassan narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids one in distress, Allah records for him seventy-three merits: one of them by which Allah sets right his affairs of this world and the Hereafter, and seventy-two in ranks."
"4268","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Tabuk, and the sun rose with a radiance, rays, and light the like of which we had never seen it rise with before. Gabriel came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Gabriel, why do I see the sun today rising with a radiance, light, and rays I never saw it rise with before? He said: That is because Mu'awiyah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Laythi died in Medina today, and Allah sent to him a thousand angels to pray over him. He said: And for what is that? He said: He said: He used to recite {Say: He is Allah, the One} much, night and day, in his walking, his standing and his sitting. Is it pleasing to you, O Messenger of Allah, that I fold the earth for you so you may pray over him? He said: Yes. So he prayed over him."
"4269","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Sami narrated to us, at Abadan, Uthman ibn al-Haytham, the muezzin of the congregational mosque at Basra in my view, narrated to us, from Mahbub ibn Hilal, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Gabriel descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Mu'awiyah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Laythi has died; would you like to pray over him? He said: Yes. He said: He struck the earth with his wing, and no tree nor hill remained but it sank low, and he raised his bier. He looked at him and said the takbir over him, and behind him were two rows of angels, in each row seventy thousand angels. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Gabriel, by what did he attain this station with Allah? He said: By his love of {Say: He is Allah, the One} and his reciting it going and coming, standing and sitting, and in every state."
"4270","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Zarwan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he washed his face, he took a handful of water and ran it through his beard from underneath, and said: Thus my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, commanded me."
"4271","Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Zufar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz, who heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his wife, let him fulfil her due; if he finishes before her, let him not hurry her."
"4272","Ibn Jami' Muhammad Abu Abdullah ibn Abi Kamil narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs, and with Uthman for the early part of his rule."
"4273","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dihqan, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to eat with his left hand or drink with his left hand."
"4274","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Abdullah ibn Dihqan, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."
"4275","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dihqan, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to eat with his left hand or drink with his left hand."
"4276","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Maysarah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy prophets have passed by the rock of al-Rawha', barefoot, wearing cloaks, heading for the Ancient House, among them Musa, the Prophet of Allah, blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4277","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Salm al-Alawi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the verse of the veil was revealed, I would enter as I used to enter, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Stay behind, my little son."
"4278","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Salm al-Alawi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A dish containing pumpkin was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he liked it. He said: I saw him inserting his finger seeking the pumpkin. He said: A man entered upon him, and he saw upon him a trace of yellow dye, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked it. He would never confront a man to his face with something he disliked. When he stood up, he said to some of the people: If only you would tell this man to leave off this yellow dye."
"4279","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: How will the people be gathered upon their faces? He said: The One who made them walk upon their feet is able to make them walk upon their faces."
"4280","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Abu Dawud al-A'ma, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: How will the people be gathered upon their faces? He said: The One who made them walk upon their feet is able to make them walk upon their faces."
"4281","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asamm, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar would not curtail the takbir."
"4282","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asamm, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman would complete the takbir when they raised and when they lowered."
"4283","al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Nawfal, who said: We entered upon Anas and said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits: whoever has them is made forbidden to the Fire, and the Fire is made forbidden to him: faith in Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and that being cast into the Fire and burned is dearer to him than returning to disbelief."
"4284","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khalid ibn Abi Tawil al-Qurashi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever keeps guard for a night on the seacoast is better than the worship of a man among his family for a thousand years, the year being three hundred and sixty days, each day being a thousand years."
"4285","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a funeral, and he saw some women. He said: Do you carry him? They said: No. He said: Do you bury him? They said: No. He said: Then go back, laden with sin and without reward."
"4286","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Ash'ath al-Huddani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Your Lord said: Whoever's two precious things I take away, then he is patient and seeks reward, his recompense is Paradise."
"4287","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Hanzalah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in the dawn prayer after bowing. He said: I heard him supplicating in his qunut against the disbelievers. He said: And I heard him saying: And make their hearts like the hearts of disbelieving women."
"4288","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Anas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, should some of us bow to others when we meet? He said: No. He said: Should some of us embrace others? He said: No. He said: Should some of us shake hands with others? He said: Shake hands."
"4289","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, from Anas: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he wiped her face. They used to come to him and he would wipe their faces and supplicate for them. She said: O Messenger of Allah, lower your hand. He said: So he pushed her away and said: Away from me."
"4290","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, who said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Abdullah saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, should some of us bow to others when we meet? He said: No. I said: Should some of us embrace others? He said: No. He said: Should some of us shake hands with one another? He said: Yes."
"4291","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Anbasah al-Qass narrated to me, Hanzalah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lifespan of the fly is forty days, and all flies are in the Fire."
"4292","Salih ibn Harb Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of these two trees, garlic and onion, let him not come near our place of prayer. And let him come to me so I may wipe his face and seek protection for him."
"4293","Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Husayn ibn Abi Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Umm Sulaym and prayed a voluntary prayer in her house. He said: O Umm Sulaym, when you have prayed the prescribed prayer, say: Glory be to Allah ten times, and Allah is Greatest ten times, then ask whatever you wish, for He will say to you: Yes, three times."
"4294","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, from Dirar ibn Muslim, who said: I heard him mention it, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me, saying: O Anas, perform ablution fully and your life will be lengthened. O Anas, pray the forenoon prayer, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning before you. O Anas, greet the people of your house and your merits will increase. O Anas, greet whomever you meet of my community and your merits will increase. O Anas, pray much by night and day and your two guardian angels will love you. O Anas, spend the night in a state of purity, for if you die, you die a martyr. O Anas, honor the elder and have mercy on the young."
"4295","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, who said: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to me, who said: Yusuf ibn Ibrahim al-Tamimi narrated to me that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which of your household is dearest to you? He said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn. He said: He used to say to Fatimah: Call my two sons to me, and he would smell them and draw them to himself."
"4296","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Shubayl ibn Azrah narrated to us, who said: Qatadah and I entered upon Anas ibn Malik, and Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the righteous companion is that of the perfume seller: if nothing of his reaches you, his scent will reach you. And the likeness of the evil companion is that of the blacksmith: if nothing of his reaches you, his smoke will reach you."
"4297","Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn Maysarah narrated to us, al-Sakan ibn Isma'il al-Asamm narrated to us, Ziyad narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who guides to good is like its doer, and Allah loves the aiding of the distressed."
"4298","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Numayri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended a high place on earth, he would say: O Allah, to You belongs loftiness above every loftiness, and to You belongs praise in every state."
"4299","Nafi' ibn Khalid al-Tahi and Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, both saying: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Qays, narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Numayri, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, small or large, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."
"4300","Abu al-Jahm al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Ziyad al-Numayri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a tree and shook it until as much of its leaves as Allah willed fell. Then he said: Pains and afflictions remove the sins of the son of Adam faster than my shaking of this tree."
"4301","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, at Balhujaym in Basra, Adi ibn Abi Umarah al-Jarmi narrated to me, Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he entered a house of the houses of Banu al-Najjar, and came out to us with his color changed. He said: Whose are these graves? They said: Graves; they died in the pre-Islamic age. He said: Then he turned to us and said: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I have seen their bodies, how they are punished in their graves."
"4302","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Adi ibn Abi Umarah narrated to us, Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan places his muzzle upon the heart of the son of Adam; if he remembers Allah, he withdraws, and if he forgets, he swallows his heart. That is the whispering retreater."
"4303","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim informed me, who said: I heard Ziyad al-Numayri narrating from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man of those before you was going out in two cloaks, strutting in them, Allah commanded the earth and it seized him, and he keeps sinking into it until the Day of Resurrection."
"4304","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim Abu Sa'id narrated to us, who said: Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Fire complained to its Lord and said: My Lord, parts of me have consumed parts of me. So He made for it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. The severity of the heat you feel is its heat, and the severity of the cold you feel is from its extreme cold."
"4305","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us, who said: Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to me - Abu Janab said: He swore three oaths by Allah, besides Whom there is no god, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, that he heard Anas ibn Malik, and he swore by Allah, besides Whom there is no god, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Intercession is for the people of major sins of my community."
"4306","And from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I am the master of the children of Adam, without pride. I am the first for whom the earth will split open, without pride. I am the first to take hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise, without pride. And the banner of praise is in my hand, without pride."
"4307","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Abdullah ibn Jabr, from Anas, who said: There was a Jewish youth who served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He fell ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He began to look at his father, who said to him: Say as Muhammad says to you. He said it, then died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Pray over your companion."
"4308","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Khalid, who is among Banu Dalan, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Abdullah ibn Jabr al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A mudd of water suffices one of you for ablution, and a sa' for bathing."
"4309","Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb and Abu Sa'id al-Qawariri narrated to us, the wording being Abu Khaythamah's, both saying: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr, who said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign of the believer is love of the Ansar, and the sign of the hypocrite is hatred of the Ansar."
"4310","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr, who said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and one of his wives would bathe from a single vessel."
"4311","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, who said: Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created the earth, it began to shake. So He created the mountains and cast them upon it, and it settled. The angels marveled at the creation of the mountains and said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation harder than the mountains? He said: Yes, iron. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation harder than iron? He said: Yes, fire. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation harder than fire? He said: Yes, water. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation harder than water? He said: Yes, wind. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation harder than wind? He said: Yes, the human who gives charity with his right hand and hides it from his left."
"4312","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Ibn Abi Nushbah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things are of the foundation of Islam: withholding from whoever says: There is no god but Allah - not declaring him a disbeliever for a sin, nor expelling him from Islam for a deed; jihad continues from the time Allah sent me until the last of my community fights the Dajjal - neither the tyranny of a tyrant nor the justice of a just ruler annuls it; and faith in all the decrees."
"4313","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Nushbah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things are of the foundation of faith: withholding from whoever says: There is no god but Allah - not declaring him a disbeliever for a sin, nor expelling him from Islam for an act; jihad continues from the time Allah sent me until my community fights the Dajjal - neither the tyranny of a tyrant nor the justice of a just ruler annuls it; and faith in all the decrees."
"4314","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Shurayh, from Abu Bahr, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How wonderful is the believer: Allah decrees no decree for him but it is good for him."
"4315","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Anas, who said: You do deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins."
"4316","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place, he would not depart from it until he bade it farewell with two rak'ahs."
"4317","Sufyan ibn Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Sa'd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and stopped at a place, and wanted to depart, he would bid the place farewell with two rak'ahs."
"4318","Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O my little son."
"4319","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abu al-Abyad, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We used to pray the afternoon prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the sun was white and high. I would go to my clan and find them sitting, and I would say to them: Stand and pray, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prayed."
"4320","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate with the people of a house, he would say: May the fasting break fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels pray upon you."
"4321","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast with the people of a house, he would say: May the fasting break fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you."
"4322","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast with a people, he would say: May the fasting break fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you."
"4323","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Murrah informed me that Yahya ibn Abi Kathir al-Yamami narrated to him, from Anas ibn Malik: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast with the people of a house, he would say: May the fasting break fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you."
"4324","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, who said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to me, from Umar ibn Dhakwan, from Dawud ibn Bakr, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there will be sinful rulers who pray the prayer outside its time. When they do that, pray the prayer in its time, and make your prayer with them voluntary."
"4325","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, who said: I heard Anas saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place, he would not depart until he prayed the noon prayer. He said: Muhammad ibn Amr said to him: Even if it is midday? He said: Even if it is midday."
"4326","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place, he would not depart until he prayed the noon prayer. Muhammad ibn Amr said to him: O Abu Hamzah, even if it is midday? He said: Even if it is midday."
"4327","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Hamzah al-Aidhi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place, he would not depart from it until he prayed the noon prayer. He said: A man said to him: Even if it is midday? He said: Even if it is midday."
"4328","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Attab, freedman of Hurmuz, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey. He said: As much as you are able."
"4329","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah, from Abu al-Mukhayyis al-Yashkuri, from Anas ibn Malik: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so, your freedman, has been martyred. He said: No indeed; I saw upon him a cloak he had misappropriated on such-and-such day."
"4330","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, who said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman al-Madini narrated to me, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the sun had declined."
"4331","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Anas ibn Malik informed him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the afternoon prayer in the time a man would go to Banu Harithah ibn al-Harith and return before sunset, and in the time a man would slaughter a camel and divide it before sunset. He would not pray the Friday prayer until the sun had declined, and when he set out for Mecca he would pray the noon prayer at al-Shajarah as two rak'ahs."
"4332","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, who said: Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to invite him, and he had prepared food for him. He said: I came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with the people. He said: He looked at me and I felt shy. I said: Answer Abu Talhah. He said to the people: Stand up. Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, I only prepared something for you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touched it and invoked blessing in it. He said: Admit a group of my companions, ten. He said: Eat. He brought out for them something between his fingers, and they ate until they were full, and went out. He kept admitting ten and sending out ten until none of them remained but entered and ate until full. He said: Then he prepared it, and it was as it was when they had eaten from it."
"4333","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah and Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is pleased with a servant who eats a meal or drinks a drink and praises Him for it."
"4334","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, who said: Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah narrated to me, from Anas, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for nine years. I do not know that he ever said to me: Why did you do such-and-such? Nor did he ever find fault with me for anything."
"4335","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is pleased with a servant who takes a bite and praises Allah for it, or drinks a drink."
"4336","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Anas, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for nine years. I do not know that he ever said to me: Why did you do such-and-such? Nor did he ever find fault with me for anything."
"4337","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mansur and Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is like half the prayer of one standing."
"4338","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Aban ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Rawahah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray the forenoon prayer except when returning from a journey or setting out."
"4339","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, who said: al-Rabi' ibn Sulaym narrated to me, who said: Abu Amr, freedman of Anas ibn Malik, narrated to me that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards his tongue, Allah covers his faults. Whoever restrains his anger, Allah withholds His punishment from him. Whoever offers his excuse to Allah, Allah accepts his excuse."
"4340","Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Nufay', from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no one on the Day of Resurrection, rich or poor, but will wish that he had only been given sustenance in this world."
"4341","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, who said: Mu'adh ibn Harmalah al-Azdi narrated to me, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon the people a time when the people receive widespread rain, but the earth will grow nothing."
"4342","Abdullah ibn Awn narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wealthy person but will wish on the Day of Resurrection that he had only been given sustenance in this world."
"4343","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, who said: I heard Shu'bah mentioning, from Abu Maslamah al-Azdi, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in his sandals? He said: Yes."
"4344","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-Muqri, narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, who said: al-Dahhak ibn Shurahbil al-Akki narrated to me, from A'yan al-Basri, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves a debt, it is upon Allah and His Messenger."
"4345","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Isma'il, from Umarah ibn Asim, who said: I entered the house of Anas ibn Malik and asked him about nabidh. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gourd vessel and the tar-coated vessel. I said: And the hantam? He repeated it to me. We said: What is the hantam? He said: The green jar. Anas ibn Malik said: O slave-girl, bring me that green jar. She brought him a jar, and he poured for me in it a cup of nabidh, and I drank it. Then he said: I never saw a green jar until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, but the hantam are green jars that used to come to us from Egypt. Then the slave-girl came to him and said: The prayer, may Allah keep you well. He said: Which prayer? She said: The afternoon prayer. I said: I already prayed it before entering to you. He said: Keep away from me; the afternoon has not yet come. Then she returned to him, and he said to her like his first saying. Then she returned to him and spoke to him. He said: I have heard what you said; hand me water for ablution, for the people pray this prayer before its time. Then he prayed."
"4346","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Asma al-Sayqal, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We set out raising our voices with the pilgrimage. When we reached Mecca, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to make it an umrah, and said: Had I faced of my affair what I have now seen behind me, I would have made it an umrah. But I have driven the sacrificial animal, and I have joined the pilgrimage and the umrah."
"4347","Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two eyes the Fire will never touch: an eye that spent the night guarding the Muslims for the sake of Allah, and an eye that wept from fear of Allah."
"4348","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib, from Abu Talhah al-Asadi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and saw a lofty dome. He said: What is this? His companions said to him: This belongs to a man of the Ansar. He kept it in himself. When its owner came to the Messenger of Allah and greeted among the people, he turned away from him. He did that with him repeatedly, until the man recognized the anger in him and the turning away from him. He complained of that to his companions and said: By Allah, I find the look of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strange; I do not know what has been said about me and what I have done? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and saw your dome. He said: Whose is this? We told him. He went back to his dome and leveled it to the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day and did not see the dome. He said: What happened to the dome that was here? He said: Its owner complained to us of your turning away from him, so we told him, and he demolished it. He said: Every building that is built is a calamity upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection, except what is indispensable."
"4349","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, Abu al-Umays narrated to us, Abu Talhah narrated to us, who said: Anas came to Kufa. He said: The people came to him and said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said, while saying: Away from me, O people, until they pressed him against the wall of the palace. Then he said: O people, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. O people, turn away from me. So they turned away."
"4350","Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bakhtari al-Wasiti Abu Abdullah al-Makfuf narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever marries has been given half of worship."
"4351","1595 - (4351) - Narrated Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated Hammad, narrated Mabad ibn Hilal al-Anazi, he said: A group of the people of Basra gathered, and I was among them, and we came to Anas ibn Malik and sought intercession to him through Thabit al-Bunani, so we entered upon him, and he seated Thabit with him on the bed, and I said: Do not ask him about anything other than this hadith. Thabit said: O Abu Hamza, your brothers from the people of Basra have come asking you about the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about intercession. He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, people will surge into one another, then Adam will be approached, and they will say: O Adam, intercede for your offspring. He will say: I am not for it, but go to Ibrahim, for he is the close friend of Allah. Then Ibrahim will be approached, and he will say: I am not for it, but upon you is Musa, for he is the one spoken to by Allah. Then Musa, the chosen of Allah, will be approached, and he will say: I am not for it, but upon you is Isa, for he is the Spirit of Allah and His Word. Then Isa will be approached, and he will say: I am not for it, but upon you is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I will be approached, and I will say: I am for it. So I will set out and ask permission upon my Lord, and permission will be given to me, and I will stand before Him in a station, and I will be inspired therein with praises that I cannot do now, and I will praise Him with those praises, then I will fall to Him prostrating. Then it will be said to me: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession. Then I will say: My Lord, my nation, my nation. Then it will be said to me: Go, and whoever has in his heart the weight of a grain of wheat or barley of faith, then bring him out. So I will go and do so, then I will return and praise Him with those praises, then fall to Him prostrating. Then it will be said: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession. Then I will say: My Lord, my nation, my nation. Then it will be said to me: Go, and whoever has in his heart the weight of an atom or mustard seed of faith, then bring him out of it. So I will go and do so, then I will return and praise Him with those praises, then fall to Him prostrating. Then it will be said: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession. Then I will say: My Lord, my nation, my nation. Then it will be said to me: Go, and whoever has in his heart less than less than the weight of a mustard grain of faith, then bring him out of the Fire, of the Fire, of the Fire. When we returned from Anas, I said to my companions: What about al-Hasan? And he was in hiding in the house of Abu Khalifa among Abd al-Qays. So we came to him and entered upon him, and we said: We came from your brother Anas, and we did not hear the like of what he narrated to us about intercession. He said: How did he narrate to you? So we narrated the hadith to him until when we reached, he said: More! We said: He did not add to us beyond this. He said: He had narrated this hadith to us when he was all together, he narrated to me twenty years ago, and he has indeed left something, and I do not know whether the old man forgot or disliked to narrate it to you lest you rely. He narrated to me, then he said in the fourth time: Then I will return and fall to Him prostrating, then I will praise with those praises. Then it will be said to me: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession. Then I will say: My Lord, permit regarding whoever said: There is no god but Allah, truthfully by it. He said: Then it will be said: It is not for you, but by My Might, My Pride and My Greatness, I shall surely bring out of it whoever said: There is no god but Allah. He said: So I bear witness upon al-Hasan that he narrated this hadith to us on the day Anas narrated."
"4352","1597 - (4352) - Narrated Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated Uqba ibn Abd Allah al-Rifai al-Asamm, from al-Jad Abi Uthman, he said: Anas ibn Malik prayed in the mosque of Banu Rifaa here, and he ordered a man from his companions to call the adhan, and he prayed the dawn prayer with them. When he finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed with his companions would turn to the people and say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a deed that disgraces me, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from wealth that makes me transgress, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a companion who ruins me, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a matter that distracts me, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty that makes me forget."
"4353","1598 - (4353) - Narrated Muhammad ibn Bahr, narrated Muhammad ibn Yala, narrated Anbasa ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Alaq, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take dinner even with a handful of inferior dates, for leaving dinner is a cause of decay."
"4354","1599 - (4354) - Narrated Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Ghubari, narrated Jafar, narrated al-Jad Abu Uthman al-Yashkuri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Umm Sulaym heard the speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: May my father and mother be for you, O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate Allah for him with some supplications. Anas said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for me with three supplications; I have seen two in this world, and I hope to see the third in the Hereafter."
"4355","1600 - (4355) - Narrated Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated Hammad, from al-Jad Abi Uthman, he said: Anas ibn Malik passed by us in the mosque of Banu Thalaba and said: Have you prayed? He said: We said: Yes, and that was the dawn prayer. Then he ordered a man, who called the adhan and iqama, then he prayed with his companions."
"4356","1601 - (4356) - Narrated Ammar Abu Yasir, narrated Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai, narrated al-Jad Abu Uthman, narrated Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consummated marriage with one of his wives. He said: So Umm Sulaym made hays for him, then put it in a tawr (a vessel), then said to me: Go with this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), convey to him greetings from us, and inform him that this from us is little for him. Anas said: And they were that day in severe hardship. He said: So I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym has sent this to you, and she conveys greetings to you, and says: This from us to you is little. He said: So he looked at it and said: Put it down. He said: So I put it down. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go and invite so-and-so and so-and-so, until he named many men, and whomever you meet. He said: So I came while the house, the suffa, and the chamber were full of people."
"4357","Musnad Aisha 1 - (4357) - Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, narrated Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated Jarir ibn Hazim, narrated Nafi, from a freedwoman of Fakih ibn al-Mughira, that she entered upon Aisha and saw in her house a spear placed. I said: O Mother of the Believers, what do you do with this spear? She said: We kill with it these geckos, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that when Ibrahim was thrown into the fire, there was no creature on earth except it extinguished from him, other than the gecko; it would blow upon him. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to kill it. He said: And Abd al-Rahman al-Siraj informed me that her name was Saiba; Shayban said: meaning the name of the freedwoman of Fakih."
"4358","2 - (4358) - Narrated Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated Jarir, narrated Nafi, from a freedwoman of Fakih ibn al-Mughira, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the snakes that are in houses, except the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they obliterate sights and kill the children of pregnant women in their bellies; and whoever does not kill them is not from us."
"4359","3 - (4359) - Narrated Shayban, narrated Jarir, narrated al-Amash, from Abi al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the woman gives charity from her husband's house without causing corruption, she has her reward, and her husband has the reward of what he earned, and she has the reward of what she intended, and the storekeeper has the like of that."
"4360","4 - (4360) - Narrated Shayban, narrated Mahdi ibn Maymun, narrated Abu Uthman al-Ansari, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and whatever intoxicates in a faraq (large measure), a handful of it is forbidden."
"4361","5 - (4361) - Narrated Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi, from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad)."
"4362","6 - (4362) - Narrated Abd al-Ala, from Malik, from Abi al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, who was an orphan in the care of Urwa, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad)."
"4363","7 - (4363) - Narrated Abd al-Ala, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, that Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you not seen that when your people built the Kaba they fell short of the foundations of Ibrahim? She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not return it upon the foundations of Ibrahim? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the recentness of your people with disbelief. He said: Then Abd Allah ibn Umar said: If Aisha heard this from the Messenger of Allah, I do not see that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left touching the two corners that adjoin the Hijr except that the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrahim."
"4364","8 - (4364) - Narrated Abd al-Ala, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: I do not mind whether I prayed in the Hijr or in the House."
"4365","9 - (4365) - Narrated Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated Tayyib ibn Salman, he said: I heard Amra say: I heard the Mother of the Believers say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays Fajr - or he said: the morning prayer - then sits in his place and does not engage in any worldly matter, and remembers Allah until he prays Duha four rakats, he exits his sins as on the day his mother bore him, with no sin upon him."
"4366","10 - (4366) - Narrated Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated Tayyib ibn Salman, he said: Amra said: I heard the Mother of the Believers say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Duha four rakats, not separating between them with speech."
"4367","11 - (4367) - Narrated Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated Tayyib ibn Salman, he said: I heard Amra say: And I heard Aisha say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would forbid uninterrupted fasting (wisal), and would order hastening the breaking of fast and delaying the sahur."
"4368","12 - (4368) - Narrated Shayban, narrated Abu al-Rabi al-Samman, narrated Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Growth of hair in the nose is a security from leprosy."
"4369","13 - (4369) - Narrated Shayban, narrated Harb ibn Surayj, he said: Zaynab bint Yazid ibn Wasiq al-Atakiyya narrated to me that she heard Aisha say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The former nations are a hundred nations; when they testify good for a servant, Paradise becomes due for him, and my nation is the fiftieth among them as a nation; when they testify good for a servant, Paradise becomes due for him. And Zaynab said: A man from the devotees of the people of Sham called Shahr ibn Hawshab said: What was the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O Mother of the Believers? She said: The Quran, my son. She said: Then Shahr said: It suffices you, and who can bear the Quran? She said: Whom Allah empowers, my son."
"4370","14 - (4370) - Narrated Shayban, narrated Abu Awana, from al-Amash, from Abi al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr from every part of the night, then his witr ended at sahar (pre-dawn)."
"4371","15 - (4371) - Narrated Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated Ismail ibn Zakariyya, narrated al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us choice, so we chose him, and he did not count it as divorce."
"4372","16 - (4372) - Narrated Abu al-Rabi, narrated Ismail ibn Zakariyya, narrated al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aisha, with the like of it."
"4373","17 - (4373) - Narrated Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim, narrated Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Budayl ibn Maysara, from Abi al-Jawza, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not add in the two rakats beyond the tashahhud."
"4374","18 - (4374) - Narrated Abu Mamar, narrated Ali ibn Hashim, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Amra, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is forbidden by breastfeeding is what is forbidden by birth."
"4375","19 - (4375) - Narrated Abu Mamar, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never struck a woman ever, nor struck a servant of his ever, nor struck anything with his hand ever, except that he strives in the path of Allah; and nothing was taken from him that he avenged from its doer, except that the sanctities of Allah are violated, then he avenges."
"4376","20 - (4376) - Narrated Abu Mamar, narrated Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim, from his father, from Muslim ibn Qurt, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to the privy, let him clean with three stones, for they suffice him."
"4377","21 - (4377) - Narrated Yahya ibn Main, narrated Abda, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: Hassan ibn Thabit sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to lampoon the polytheists. He said: Then how about my lineage among them? He said: I shall surely draw you out from them as a hair is drawn from dough."
"4378","22 - (4378) - Narrated Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, narrated Abda, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wisal (uninterrupted fasting). They said: O Messenger of Allah, you practice wisal? He said: It is only a mercy by which Allah has shown you mercy; I am not like you. I remain with Allah, He feeds me and gives me drink."
"4379","23 - (4379) - Narrated Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, narrated Abda and Humayd, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, he said: Aisha narrated to me that the hand of a thief was not cut in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except for the price of a shield or a buckler."
"4380","24 - (4380) - Narrated Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, narrated Abd Allah ibn Idris, from Hizam ibn Hisham, my father informed me, from Aisha, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angry over what happened in the affair of Banu Kab with an anger I had not seen him angry with for a long time, and he said: May Allah not aid me if I do not aid Banu Kab. She said: And he said to me: Tell Abu Bakr and Umar to prepare for this expedition. He said: So they came to Aisha and said: Where does the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intend? He said: She said: I saw him angry over what happened in the affair of Banu Kab with an anger I had not seen him angry with for ages."
"4381","25 - (4381) - Narrated Yahya ibn Main, narrated Said ibn al-Hakam, narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, from Amra bint Abd al-Rahman, she said: There was in Mecca a jesting woman, and she stayed with a woman like her. That reached Aisha, so she said: My beloved spoke truth; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Souls are troops assembled; what they recognize of them unites, and what they dislike of them differs. He said: And I know only that he said in the hadith: And that woman is not known."
"4382","26 - (4382) - Narrated Abd al-Ala, I read upon Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet, that she said: He was never given choice between two matters except he chose the easier of them, so long as it was not sin; if it was sin, he was the farthest of people from it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never avenged for himself, except that the sanctity of Allah is violated, then he avenges for Allah by it."
"4383","27 - (4383) - Narrated Musab ibn Abd Allah ibn Musab al-Zubayri, Ibn al-Darawardi narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a boy who had been treated with throat compression, and said: Upon what do you kill your children? Upon you is Indian costus with water, then administer it through his nose."
"4384","28 - (4384) - Narrated Musab ibn Abd Allah, Hisham ibn Abd Allah ibn Ikrima narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek provision in the hidden parts of the earth."
"4385","29 - (4385) - Narrated Musab ibn Abd Allah, Ibn al-Darawardi narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat and drink until Bilal calls the adhan."
"4386","30 - (4386) - Narrated Musab, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to me, from Musab ibn Thabit, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves that when one of you does a deed, he perfects it."
"4387","31 - (4387) - Narrated Musab, he said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to me, from Musab ibn Thabit, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring the qibla near (face it directly)."
"4388","32 - (4388) - Narrated Musab ibn Abd Allah, narrated Ibrahim ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed tahajjud in his house, and Abbad ibn Bishr prayed tahajjud in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice and said: O Aisha, is this Abbad ibn Bishr? I said: Yes. He said: O Allah, have mercy on Abbad."
"4389","33 - (4389) - Narrated Musab, narrated Ibrahim ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, from Aisha, she said: Three from the Ansar, all from Banu Abd al-Ashhal, none was counted as having precedence over them after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Sad ibn Muadh, Usayd ibn Hudayr, and Abbad ibn Bishr."
"4390","34 - (4390) - Narrated Harun ibn Maruf, narrated Abd Allah ibn Wahb, he said: And Amr informed me, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, that Abu Muslim al-Khawlani performed Hajj and entered upon Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She began asking him about Sham and its cold, and he began informing her. She said: How do they endure its cold? He said: O Mother of the Believers, they drink a drink called tila. She said: Allah spoke truth and my beloved conveyed; I heard my beloved say: Some people of my nation will drink wine, calling it by other than its name. She said: And how do the women do? He said: They enter bathhouses. She said: Allah spoke truth and my beloved conveyed; I heard my beloved say: There is no woman who puts off her garment in other than her house except Allah removes covering from her."
"4391","35 - (4391) - Narrated Harun ibn Maruf, narrated Damra, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his ihram, and I perfumed him for his release from ihram, with a perfume unlike this perfume of yours, meaning: it has no lasting trace."
"4392","36 - (4392) - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm, narrated Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Abi Sad, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abi al-Bakhtari al-Tai, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The protection of the Muslims is one; if a slave-girl among them grants protection, do not betray her, for every treacherous one has a banner by which he will be known on the Day of Resurrection."
"4393","37 - (4393) - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrated Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, Yunus ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Zuhri, Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, he said: A man sat in the courtyard of Aisha's chamber and began talking. He said: Then Aisha said: Were I not glorifying Allah I would have said to him: The Messenger of Allah would not string speech as you string; the speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was distinct, understood by hearts."
"4394","38 - (4394) - Narrated Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi, narrated Hassan ibn Ibrahim, narrated Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: I would twist the garlands of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he sends the offering while he is staying with us, not avoiding anything that the muhrim avoids. It reached us that Ziyad sent an offering and stripped (for ihram); so she said: And did he have a Kaba to circumambulate when he wore clothes? For we know of none upon whom clothes become forbidden then become lawful until he circumambulates the Kaba."
"4395","39 - (4395) - Narrated Suwayd ibn Said, narrated Ibn Abi Zaida, from his father, from Musab ibn Shayba, from Musafi ibn Abd Allah, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, that a woman said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does the woman wash if she has a wet dream and sees water? He said: Yes. Then Aisha said to her: May your hands be dusty. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her; is resemblance except from that? If her water overcomes the man's water, the man resembles his maternal uncles; and if the man's water overcomes the woman's water, he resembles him."
"4396","40 - (4396) - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Samina al-Basri, narrated Abd al-Wahhab, narrated Yunus, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Aisha, she said: We would make nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin tied at its top, having a spout; we would make it in the morning and he drinks it in the evening, and we make it in the evening and he drinks it in the morning."
"4397","41 - (4397) - Narrated Masruq ibn al-Marzuban, narrated Ibn al-Mubarak, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to travel, he would draw lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, he would take her out."
"4398","42 - (4398) - Narrated Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilaba, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No Muslim dies and a nation of Muslims reaching a hundred pray upon him and intercede for him except they are granted intercession for him."
"4399","43 - (4399) - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Aruzzi, narrated Abu Zukayr al-Madani, he said: I heard Hisham ibn Urwa mention, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat unripe dates with ripe dates, for when the son of Adam eats, Satan gets angry, saying: The son of Adam remains until he ate the old with the new."
"4400","44 - (4400) - Narrated Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated Hammad ibn Salama, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the boy until he has a wet dream, and from the insane until he regains sense."
"4401","45 - (4401) - Narrated Surayj ibn Yunus, narrated Abu Muawiya, from Asim, from Tubala bint Yazid al-Abshamiyya, from Aisha, she said: Nabidh would be made for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin; we would take a handful of raisins or a handful of dates and throw it in the waterskin, then pour water upon it at night and he drinks it in daytime, or in daytime and he drinks it at night."
"4402","46 - (4402) - Narrated Surayj, narrated Abu Muawiya, narrated Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white garments, Sahuliyya of cotton, with no shirt nor turban in them. As for the hulla (suit), the people were only made to confuse about it that it was bought for him to be shrouded in, then the hulla was left. Then Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr took it. He said: I shall keep it to be shrouded in. Then he said: If Allah had been pleased with it for His Messenger he would have been shrouded in it. So he sold it and gave its price in charity."
"4403","47 - (4403) - Narrated Surayj, narrated Abu Muawiya, narrated Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from a journey. She said: So I hung upon my door a thin curtain with winged horses on it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, he said to me: Remove it."
"4404","48 - (4404) - Narrated Surayj ibn Yunus, narrated Abu Muawiya, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The bedding of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon which he slept at night was of leather stuffed with fiber."
"4405","49 - (4405) - Narrated al-Hakam ibn Musa, narrated Hiql, from al-Awzai, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Amra bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurara, from Aisha, she said: Umm Habiba bint Jahsh had prolonged bleeding, and she was under Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf for seven years. She complained of that to the Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When menstruation comes, leave prayer; when it goes, wash then pray. Aisha said: So she would wash at every prayer, and she would sit in a tub for her sister Zaynab bint Jahsh until the redness of blood would overcome the water."
"4406","50 - (4406) - Narrated Ghassan ibn al-Rabi, from Thabit meaning Ibn Yazid, from Burd, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: I opened the door while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying voluntary prayer, and the door was in the qibla. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked to his right or to his left until he opened the door, then returned to his prayer."
"4407","51 - (4407) - Narrated Hudba, narrated Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution, then kiss, then pray, and not renew ablution."
"4408","52 - (4408) - Narrated Hawthara ibn Ashras Abu Amir, Jafar ibn Kaysan Abu Maruf informed me, from Amra al-Adawiyya, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation perishes only by stabbing and plague. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we know stabbing; what is plague? He said: A swelling like the swelling of camels; the one who stays in it is like a martyr, and the one who flees from it is like one fleeing from battle."
"4409","53 - (4409) - Narrated Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I had hung a curtain with images. His face changed color, then he took the curtain and tore it. Then he said: Among the severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah."
"4410","54 - (4410) - Narrated Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama al-Umari, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Amra, from Aisha, she said: Umm Habiba bint Jahsh came, and she had prolonged bleeding for seven years, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She complained of that to him and sought his ruling in it. He said: This is not menstruation, but this is a vein. So wash, then pray. He said: So she would wash for every prayer, and she would sit in the tub and the redness of blood would overcome the water, then she prays."
"4411","Abdulaziz al-Umari narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is cut off for a quarter of a dinar and above."
"4412","Abdulaziz narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ghusl from a vessel which is the faraq. She said: And I used to perform ghusl with him from the same vessel. Ibrahim said: al-Zuhri said: And I think the faraq in those days was about five qists."
"4413","Abdulaziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to part the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the crown of his head, and I would let it hang down for him when I oiled his forelock."
"4414","Abdulaziz al-Umari narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a khamisah that had markings, then he looked at its markings once, and when he finished the prayer he said: Take this khamisah of mine to Abu Jahm, for it distracted me just now from my prayer, and bring me the anbijaniyyah of Abu Jahm."
"4415","Abdulaziz al-Umari narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: There were women among the believing women who used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrapped in their cloaks, then they would return to their houses, and they could not be recognized due to the darkness of dawn."
"4416","Ishaq and others narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that women among the believers used to pray the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrapped in their cloaks, then they would return to their families, and no one would recognize them."
"4417","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies while fasting is owed, his guardian fasts on his behalf."
"4418","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one's wealth benefited us as the wealth of Abu Bakr benefited us."
"4419","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Sad and Abd ibn Zamah disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sad said: My brother instructed me when I came to Makkah to take the son of the slave woman of Zamah, and he is my son. Abd ibn Zamah said: O Messenger of Allah, he is my brother and the son of my father's slave woman, born on my father's bed. Then he saw a clear resemblance to Utbah. He said: So he said: He is yours; the child belongs to the bed. And hide yourself from him, O Sawdah."
"4420","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the Asr prayer while the sun was still high in her chamber and the shade had not yet appeared."
"4421","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: A group of Jews sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Death be upon you. Aishah said: So I said: Upon you be death and the curse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, indeed Allah loves gentleness in every matter. She said: I said: Did you not hear what they said? He said: I said: And upon you."
"4422","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me one day delighted, saying: O Aishah, have you not seen Mujazziz al-Mudliji? He came to me and saw Usamah and Zayd covered with a blanket, their heads covered and their feet visible, and he said: These feet are related to one another."
"4423","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: The wife of Rifah al-Qurazi came to the Messenger of Allah and said: Rifah divorced me and made my divorce irrevocable, then I married Abdurrahman ibn al-Zubayr after him, but what he has is like the fringe of a garment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: Do you wish to return to Rifah? No, until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his sweetness."
"4424","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a dead person for more than three days, except for a husband."
"4425","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard recitation in it. I said: What is this? They said: Harithah ibn al-Numan. Such is righteousness, such is righteousness, such is righteousness. And he was dutiful to his mother."
"4426","Abdulala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Salamah, he said: Abdurrahman performed ablution in the presence of Aishah, and she said: O Abdurrahman, perform ablution thoroughly, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"4427","Abdulala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdurrahman, from Abu Yunus the freed slave of Aishah, that Aishah said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was standing behind the door listening. He said: Prayer overtakes me while I am in a state of janabah, and I intend to fast. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer overtakes me too while I am in a state of janabah, and I intend to fast, then I perform ghusl and fast. The man said: You are not like me; Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I hope to be the most God-fearing of you toward Allah and the most knowledgeable of you of the limits of Allah."
"4428","Abdulala narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss one of his wives while fasting, then she laughed."
"4429","Abdulala narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel, both of us sharing it together."
"4430","And with his chain, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended to perform ghusl from janabah would pour water over his hands and wash them, then perform ablution as for prayer, then dip his hands in the vessel, then take them out and insert them into his head, tracing the roots of the hair until when he had moistened the skin of the hair and it seemed to him that he had cleansed it, he would pour three handfuls of water over his head, then pour the rest over his body. And Urwah said on his own: When he washes his palms, let him wash his private part, then perform ablution as for prayer."
"4431","And from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the prayer is present and supper is served, then begin with supper."
"4432","Ali ibn al-Jad and Hudbah narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, he said: We visited Aishah, and she brought out to us a coarse waist-wrapper of the kind made in Yemen, and a cloak of those you call mulabbadah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away in these two garments."
"4433","Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Sawdah was a large-bodied woman; when she went out she stood out above the women. Umar ibn al-Khattab saw her and said to her: Look how you go out; by Allah, you are not hidden from us when you go out. So Sawdah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in his hand was a bone with meat. He said: The bone shook in his hand due to the shock of revelation, then he said: Indeed Allah has granted you permission to go out for your needs."
"4434","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: That a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My mother died suddenly, and I think that had she spoken she would have given charity. Shall I give charity on her behalf? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes."
"4435","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: Barirah came to me and said: I have contracted with my people for nine uqiyyahs, one uqiyyah each year, so help me. Aishah said to her: If your people agree that I pay it to them in one payment and your wala will be mine, I will do so. So Barirah went to her people and told them, but they refused unless the wala would be theirs. The Messenger of Allah heard that and asked her, and Aishah informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take her and stipulate the wala for them, for wala belongs only to the one who frees. Aishah said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people, praised Allah, then said: To proceed: What is the matter with men who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Whatever is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if it were a hundred conditions. And he said: The decree of Allah is most true, and the condition of Allah is most binding, and wala belongs only to the one who frees."
"4436","Abdulala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah: That Barirah was a mukatabah belonging to some people of the Ansar. She said: So I wanted to buy her and free her, so I told her to go to them and inform them. They said: If you grant us her wala, we will sell her to you. So I sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Buy her and free her, for wala belongs only to the one who pays the price. She said: She was married to a slave, and when she was freed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Choose: if you wish, remain under this slave, and if you wish, separate from him. She said: So I have separated from him. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while the pot was boiling with meat, and he said: What is this, O Aishah? I said: Barirah gave it to us as charity given to her. He said: It is charity for Barirah, and a gift for us."
"4437","Abdulala narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Abu Bakr came seeking permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was wearing the cloak of the Mother of the Believers. He gave him permission, and he fulfilled his need with him, then left. Then Umar sought permission, and he gave him permission while in that same state, and he fulfilled his need, then left. Then Uthman sought permission, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat up straight and said to Aishah: Gather your garments about you. Then he gave him permission. When he left, Aishah said to him: Why were you not concerned for Abu Bakr and Umar as you were concerned for Uthman? He said: Indeed Uthman is shy, and had I given him permission in that state I feared he would not convey his need."
"4438","Abdulala narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Murrah narrated to us, from al-Qasim, he said: Aishah said: I bought a cushion for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed it for him, but it was as if he disliked that. Aishah said: I seek refuge with Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger. He said: What is this, O Aishah? She said: So that when someone enters upon you or a delegation comes to you. He said: O Aishah, indeed the makers of these images will be punished with a punishment with which no one among the worlds is punished. It will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"4439","Abdulala narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: I heard al-Qasim narrating, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is appointed over a task and Allah intends good for him, Allah makes for him a truthful minister; if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him."
"4440","Abdulala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abdurrahman, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdurrahman, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and pointed to the moon, and said: O Aishah, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this darkness when it settles."
"4441","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Harb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Mujahid narrated to us, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wild animal that would come forward and go back, but when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, it would crouch and not move, fearing to harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4442","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abu Aqil, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated a narration one day, and a woman among them said: O Messenger of Allah, this narration is as if it is the tale of Khurafah. He said: Do you know what Khurafah is? Indeed Khurafah was a man of Udhrah whom the jinn captured in the pre-Islamic period. He stayed among them a long time, then they returned him to mankind, and he used to narrate to people the wonders he saw among them. So the people said: The tale of Khurafah."
"4443","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hasten to any voluntary prayer as he hastened to the two rakahs of Fajr, nor to any war booty."
"4444","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Thawr, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Salih, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce nor emancipation under compulsion."
"4445","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Muammal, Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent condiment vinegar is."
"4446","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Muzarrid, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The womb is suspended from the Throne, saying: Whoever connects me, Allah connects him, and whoever severs me, Allah severs him."
"4447","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdurrahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, the Bedouins bring us meat and we do not know whether they mentioned the name of Allah over it or not? He said: So mention the name yourselves over it, and eat."
"4448","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, that he asked Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah pray on a mat? For I heard in the Book of Allah: And We have made Hell a mat for the disbelievers. She said: He did not use to pray upon it."
"4449","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Abdulaziz ibn Rufay, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ikrimah, from Aishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by the pot and take a piece of meat with bone from it and eat some of it, then pray without performing ablution."
"4450","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, Hawshab ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Ghaniyyah bint al-Radi, she said: I visited the Mother of the Believers Aishah with some women of Abdulqays, and we asked her about nabidh. She said: May Allah not benefit you, O Abdulqays, with nabidh. The Messenger of Allah forbade the hantam, the dubba, and the naqir. She said: But drink from all leather skins, whatever you tie shut or hang up."
"4451","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I visited Abu Bakr and saw death upon him, and I said: Confusion, confusion. Muffled. He said to her: Do not say that, but say: And the stupor of death comes in truth; that is what you were avoiding. Then he said: On which day did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) die? She said: I said: On Monday. He said: I hope between now and the night. He said: He did not die until the evening of Tuesday night, and he was buried before morning. She said: And he had said before that: In how many garments was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded? I said: In three white Sahuli garments, with neither shirt nor turban. Then he looked at a garment in which he had been nursed during illness, in which there was a trace of saffron or red dye, and said: Wash this garment of mine and add two more garments to it and shroud me in them. She said: I said: This is worn out. He said: The living are more entitled to the new than the dead; it is only for the discharge."
"4452","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Muhammad ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) retaliating for a wrong done to him, except when something of the sacred limits of Allah was violated. When something of the sacred limits of Allah was violated, he was the most severe of them in that matter. And he was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of the two."
"4453","Al-Abbas narrated to us, Abduljabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah say: Aishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Everyone who is reckoned on that Day has perished. I said: O Messenger of Allah, for Allah says: He will be reckoned with an easy reckoning. He said: That is only the presentation, O Aishah. As for everyone whose account is scrutinized on that Day, he has perished."
"4454","Al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever supplicates against the one who wronged him - or he said: against the wrongdoer - has taken revenge."
"4455","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: I heard Aishah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say while among his Companions: I am your predecessor at the Hawd, waiting for those of you who come to me. By Allah, men will surely be cut off before reaching me, and I will say: My Lord, from me and from my ummah. Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you; they kept turning back on their heels."
"4456","Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Habib al-Muallim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of Madinah to lead the people in prayer."
"4457","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abdulmalik, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from janabah from a single vessel, both of us sharing it together, but he would begin and perform ablution."
"4458","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to wash the face of Usamah ibn Zayd one day when he was a child. She said: I had never given birth nor did I know how children are washed. She said: So I took him and washed him with a washing that was not quite proper. She said: Then he took him and began washing his face, saying: We have been treated well since you were not a girl; had you been a girl I would have adorned you and given to you."
"4459","Zakariyya narrated to us, from Hushaym, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick person, he would place his hand on the place the sick person complained of, then say: In the name of Allah, no harm, no harm; remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness. Aishah said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, I placed my hand upon him to say these words, but he pulled my hand away from him and said: O Allah, You are the Highest Companion."
"4460","Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said: I asked Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite poetry? She said: When he entered his house he would recite, saying: If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold he would seek a third to them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever turns. Wealth was only made for prayer to be performed with it and zakat to be given from it. She said: So we considered it among what was abrogated of the Quran."
"4461","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: A lizard was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not eat any of it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not feed it to the beggars? He said: I do not feed the beggars except what I eat from."
"4462","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba and the muzaffat."
"4463","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: A beggar came to her, and Aishah ordered something for him. When the servant came she called her and looked. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Does nothing go out except with your knowledge? She said: Indeed I know. He said: Do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"4464","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ata, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he had thrown the pebbles, slaughtered, and shaved, everything became lawful for him except women."
"4465","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Jahm, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet, with the like of it."
"4466","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, he said: I asked Aishah about the vessels the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade. She said: The gourd and the muzaffat: they are green pitch-coated jars brought from Egypt."
"4467","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, that Aishah said: When the chapter of al-Baqarah was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wine and usury."
"4468","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Azrah, from Humayd ibn Abdurrahman, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that she said: There was a curtain over my door with images on it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remove this, for it reminds me of the world. She said: And we had a blanket in which there was silk."
"4469","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah."
"4470","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Aishah, that al-Najashi gave to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift containing a gold ring with an Abyssinian stone. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it with a stick and handed it to Umamah as if turning away from it, and said: Adorn yourself with this."
"4471","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umm Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a gift containing a necklace of onyx. He said: I will surely give it to the most beloved of my household to me. The women said: The daughter of Abu Quhafah has gotten it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Umamah bint Zaynab and hung it around her neck."
"4472","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make me among those who, when they do good, rejoice, and when they do wrong, seek forgiveness."
"4473","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Jabr ibn Habib and Said al-Jurayri, from Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught her to say: O Allah, I ask You for all good, its immediate and its delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know. And I seek refuge in You from all evil, its immediate and its delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your servant and Prophet asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil that Your servant and Prophet sought refuge from. And I ask You for Paradise and whatever brings near to it of word or deed, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and whatever brings near to it of word or deed. And I ask You to make every decree You decree for me good."
"4474","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire and from the trial of the Fire. And I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave and from the trial of the grave. And I seek refuge in You from the False Messiah, and from laziness, old age, sin, and debt, and from the evil of the trial of wealth and poverty. O Allah, wash me of sins with the water of snow and hail. O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the East and the West."
"4475","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, that Aishah said to al-Saib: Three traits: either leave them or I will contend with you. He said: What are they? She said: Beware of rhymed speech, do not rhyme, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions did not rhyme. And when you come to people talking, do not interrupt their conversation. And do not weary people with the Book of Allah, and do not narrate on Friday except once; if you insist, then twice."
"4476","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abdurrahman ibn Hatib, that Aishah said: I brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a khazirah I had cooked for him. I said to Sawdah - with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between me and her -: Eat. She refused. I said: You will surely eat, or I will smear your face. She refused, so I put my hand in the khazirah and smeared her face. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and put his hand out for her and said to her: Smear her face. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at her. Then Umar passed by and said: O Abdullah, O Abdullah. He thought he would enter, so he said: Get up and wash your faces. Aishah said: I continued to fear Umar due to the awe of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4477","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Sad ibn Muadh was struck in his medial arm vein. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pitched a tent for him in the mosque to visit him from nearby. Sad said: O Allah, You know that the people I most love to fight are a people who denied Your Prophet, expelled him, and did such and such. And I think You have ended the war between us and them. O Allah, if You have kept any war between us and them, keep me alive for them. And if You have ended the war between us and them, then cause this wound to burst and make my death therein. Then one night while he was thus, his wound burst from his chest. Beside him were dwellers of a tent, and blood flowed until it entered the tent. They called out to them: O dwellers of the tent, what is this coming to us from your direction? They looked and behold Sad ibn Muadh's wound had burst from his chest, and his blood had a roaring and rumbling sound. He said: So he died from it."
"4478","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness: Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer. Aishah said to Hafsah: Tell him: Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and when he stands in your place the people will not hear him due to weeping. So order Umar to lead the people in prayer. Hafsah said that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer. Aishah said to Hafsah the like of her first statement. He said: Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer. Aishah repeated to Hafsah the like of her statement to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Leave me; you are indeed the companions of Yusuf. Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer."
"4479","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah with the like of it. Then Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: And what caliphate is clearer than this."
"4480","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun was still high in my chamber."
"4481","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdurrahman, that Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to perform ghusl from janabah, he would wash his hands three times, then take water with his right hand, then pour it upon his left and wash his private part until he cleansed it. Then he would wash his left hand well, then rinse his mouth three times, inhale water three times, wash his face, wash his forearms three times each, then pour water over his head three times, then wash his body. When he finished his washing, he would wash his feet."
"4482","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended to perform ghusl from janabah would perform ablution as for prayer, then insert his hand into the vessel and trace the roots of the hair with his right hand on his right side, and take with his left and trace the roots of the hair on his left side, until when he thought he had cleansed the entire skin, he would pour over his head. Hisham said: Except that before that he begins by washing his hands three times each, and by washing his private part."
"4483","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah and Asim al-Ahwal, from Muadhah al-Adawiyyah, that Aishah said: I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel. Asim said: Aishah said: And he would hasten with me in rivalry."
"4484","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, that Aishah said: I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah, from a single vessel."
"4485","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying and felt cold, and said: O Aishah, spread your cloak over me. She said: I am menstruating. He said: Is it an excuse and stinginess? Your menstruation is not in your hands."
"4486","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who suffers istihadah; shall I leave prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is only a vein, and it is not menstruation. When menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when its intensity departs, wash the blood from yourself, perform ablution, and pray."
"4487","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Yazid ibn Babanus, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take from my head while I was menstruating with a garment between me and him."
"4488","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Hand me the prayer mat. She said: I am menstruating. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your menstruation is not in your hands."
"4489","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdurrahman, that Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, he would establish it regularly."
"4490","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I lay across between him and the qiblah like the lying of a funeral bier under my blanket."
"4491","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: Have you put us in the position of dogs and donkeys! I saw myself under my cloak in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between him and the qiblah while he was praying, and I disliked to appear before him, so I would slip out from under the cloak stealthily."
"4492","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah: That a man stood at night and recited, raising his voice with the Quran. In the morning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on so-and-so; how many verses he reminded me of tonight that I had dropped."
"4493","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Amrah bint Abdurrahman al-Ansariyyah, that Aishah said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had seen of women what we see, he would have prevented them from the mosques, just as the Children of Israel prevented their women. I saw us praying Fajr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in our cloaks, then departing while none of us recognized the faces of others."
"4494","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Aishah, that she said: They differed about washing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so sleep was cast upon them, and there was none of them but his chin upon his chest. Then they were called from the side of the house: Wash him from behind his shirt. Aishah said: Had I known beforehand what I know now, none would have washed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but his wives."
"4495","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr said to Aishah: On which day did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) die? She said: On Monday. He said: What day is this? She said: Monday. He said: What Allah wills; I hope between now and the night. And he said to them: With what did you shroud him? She said: In three white Yemeni Sahuli garments with neither shirt nor turban. Abu Bakr said: Wash this garment of mine of the trace of saffron or red dye, along with two other garments. Aishah said: O father, this is worn out. He said: The living are more entitled to the new. He said: It is only for the discharge. And Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr had given them a Hibarah shawl, so the Messenger of Allah was wrapped in it, then taken out of it, and shrouded in three white Yemeni Sahuli garments. Abdullah found the shawl and said: I will surely shroud myself in something that touched the skin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said afterwards: No, by Allah, I will not shroud myself in something Allah prevented His Messenger from being shrouded in. Then Abu Bakr died on Tuesday night and was buried at night."
"4496","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited him during his illness while he was praying sitting, so they stood praying behind him. He gestured to them with his hand to sit, so they sat. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: The imam is only appointed to be followed. When he bows, bow, and when he prostrates, prostrate. If he prays standing, pray standing, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"4497","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ghusl from janabah, he would pour with his right upon his left and wash his private part - and perhaps she expressed the private part euphemistically - then perform ablution as for prayer, then insert his hand into the water, then run it through his hair. If he thought the water had reached the skin, he would pour water over his head three times, and leave a remainder in the vessel and pour it over himself after finishing."
"4498","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were shown to me in a dream. I said: When the angel brought you in a piece of silk, saying: This is your wife. When I uncovered your face, behold you were she. So I say: If it is from Allah, He will carry it out."
"4499","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the statement of Ibn Umar about wailing over the dead was mentioned in her presence. She said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abdurrahman; he heard the narration but did not retain it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said - as they passed by him with the funeral of a Jew while his family wept over him -: They are weeping, and he is being punished."
"4500","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, all your women have kunyas except me. He said: Then take a kunya by your son Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. So she was called Umm Abdullah."
"4501","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the brother of Abu Quays sought permission to enter upon her but she refused to admit him. She mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He is your paternal uncle, so admit him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, only the woman suckled me, the man did not suckle me? He said: He is your paternal uncle, so admit him."
"4502","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who fasts continuously; shall I fast while traveling? He said: Fast if you wish, and break fast if you wish."
"4503","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five harmful creatures are killed in the Haram: the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, the crow, and the vicious dog."
"4504","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: We set out coinciding with the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to enter ihram for Hajj, let him enter ihram for Hajj, and whoever wishes to enter ihram for Umrah, let him enter ihram for Umrah. So I was among those who entered ihram for Umrah. She mentioned that when she was at Sarif she menstruated. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was weeping. He said: So I said: I wish I had not come out this year. He said: Undo your head, abandon your Umrah, comb your hair, and do what the Muslims do in their Hajj. So she obeyed Allah and His Messenger. When it was the night of departure, he ordered Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr to take her out to al-Tanim. So he took her out to al-Tanim, and she entered ihram from there for Umrah."
"4505","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: It is as if I am looking at myself twisting the necklaces of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he does not refrain from anything that one in ihram refrains from."
"4506","Suwayd narrated to us, Abdulaziz, meaning al-Darawardi, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to observe itikaf, he would pray Fajr, then enter his place of itikaf. When it was the morning of the twenty-first, he left after Fajr and entered the mosque, and saw tents: the tent of Aishah - and she had sought his permission - and of Zaynab. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do they intend righteousness with these? Then he postponed his itikaf to Shawwal."
"4507","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The delegations of the Arabs crowded upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and forced him to the house of Aishah. He said: O Allah, curse them. Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, the people are ruined. He said: No, by Allah, O daughter of al-Siddiq. I have stipulated a condition with my Lord that has no revocation. I said: O Allah, I am a human who is constrained by what humans are constrained by, and hastens with what humans hasten with. So whichever person a harsh word of mine reaches, make it an expiation for him."
"4508","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah made an appointment with Gabriel in an hour he would come to him. That hour came but he did not come, and in his hand was a stick. He threw it from his hand and said: Allah does not break His promise, nor do His messengers. Then he turned and behold a puppy under the bed. He said: O Aishah, when did this dog enter here? She said: By Allah, I did not notice it. He ordered it removed, so it was taken out. Then Gabriel came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You promised me, so I sat waiting for you but you did not come. He said: The dog that was in your house prevented me; we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"4509","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, that Hafsah bint Abdurrahman narrated to him, from Aishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoin the faraah: one from every five sheep."
"4510","Suwayd narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while dying, with a cup of water beside him. He would dip his hand in the cup, then wipe his face with it, then say: O Allah, help me with the pangs of death."
"4511","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah the Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The jihad of women is Hajj."
"4512","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah the Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The swiftest good in reward is maintaining kinship ties, and the swiftest evil in punishment is transgression."
"4513","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Qays say: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting without break."
"4514","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muadhah, from Aishah, she said: Tell your husbands to wash the traces of stool and urine, for I am shy before them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do so."
"4515","Ishaq narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Harun al-Awar narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he recited: Then rest and bounty."
"4516","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The most beloved drink to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the sweet cold drink."
"4517","Ishaq narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Musab ibn Shaybah, from Talq ibn Habib, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten are of the fitrah: trimming the mustache, letting the beard grow, the siwak, inhaling water, trimming the nails, washing the knuckles, plucking the armpit, shaving the pubic hair, and cleansing with water. Waki said: Meaning istinja with water that removes urine. Zakariyya said: Musab said: And I forgot the tenth, unless it is rinsing the mouth."
"4518","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They have indeed known that what I called them to in the world is the truth. And Allah has said: Indeed you do not make the dead hear."
"4519","Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from his mother Musaykah, from Aishah, she said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not build for you a house to shade you? He said: No, Mina is a resting place for whoever arrives first."
"4520","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I bought Barirah to free her, but her people stipulated her wala. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Free her, for wala belongs to the one who frees. Her husband was free while she was enslaved, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice."
"4521","Ishaq narrated to us, Abdulmajid ibn Abdulaziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Two equivalent sheep are sacrificed for a boy, and one sheep for a girl. Aishah said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed for al-Hasan and al-Husayn two sheep each on the seventh day, and ordered that harm be removed from his head, and said: Slaughter in his name, and say: In the name of Allah, Allah is Greatest; O Allah, from You and to You; this is the aqeeqah of so-and-so. He said: In the pre-Islamic period a piece of cotton was taken and placed in the blood of the aqeeqah, then placed on his head. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to place perfume in place of blood."
"4522","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended to sleep while in a state of janabah would perform ablution as for prayer."
"4523","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful."
"4524","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I had screened myself with a curtain having images. When he saw it, his face changed color and he tore it down, and said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah."
"4525","Ishaq narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever persists upon twelve rakahs of the Sunnah apart from the obligatory prayer, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"4526","Ishaq narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray between Isha thirteen rakahs, making witr among them with five, giving salam in the fifth."
"4527","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: When a person complained, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say with his saliva, then apply it to the dust, saying: The dust of our land with the saliva of one of us; our sick is healed by the permission of our Lord."
"4528","Ishaq narrated to us, Man al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Fulan ibn Muhammad ibn Khalid, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He would not interpret anything of the Quran by his opinion, except a few verses that Gabriel taught him."
"4529","Ishaq narrated to us, Abdulwarith ibn Said narrated to us, Yazid al-Rishk narrated to us, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that she asked her: How many rakahs did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray for Duha? She said: Four rakahs, and he would add whatever Allah willed."
"4530","Ishaq narrated to us, Abdussamad ibn Abdulwarith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihzam al-Shabb narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Qasim narrated to us, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed whoever is given his share of gentleness has been given his share of the good of this world and the Hereafter. And whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has been deprived of his share of the good of this world and the Hereafter."
"4531","Ishaq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not perform ablution after ghusl."
"4532","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Talhah ibn Ubaydullah say: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaned toward me to kiss me while I was fasting. I said: I am fasting. He said: And I am fasting. Then he kissed me."
"4533","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad, he said: I heard Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deed is most beloved to Allah? He said: The most constant, even if little."
"4534","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: Aishah said: We used to hear that no prophet dies until given a choice between this world and the Hereafter. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his illness in which he died when hoarseness seized him. I heard him say: With those whom Allah has favored among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and excellent are those as companions. So I knew he had been given the choice."
"4535","Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any condition not in the Book of Allah is void, even if it were a hundred conditions."
"4536","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, he said: Aishah said: I never saw anyone suffer more severe pain than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4537","Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Makhlad ibn Khufaf, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that revenue is by liability."
"4538","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said: I visited Aishah, and she called for food for me and said to me: Eat, for whenever I eat my fill of food and wish to weep, I weep. I said: Why is that? She said: I remember the state in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the world. The Messenger of Allah never ate his fill of wheat bread twice in one day until he met Allah."
"4539","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The family of Muhammad never ate their fill of wheat food for three consecutive nights since coming to Madinah until he passed away."
"4540","Ishaq narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The family of Muhammad never ate their fill, morning or evening, of barley bread for three successive days until he met Allah."
"4541","Ishaq narrated to us, Abdussamad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah never ate his fill for two days of barley bread until he died."
"4542","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died leaving neither dinar nor dirham, nor sheep nor camel, and he did not bequeath anything."
"4543","Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Maslamah ibn Qanab narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone without Umrah."
"4544","Ishaq narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us, from Awf, from Awfa ibn Dalham al-Adawi, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take from our faces while fasting."
"4545","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from debt. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you seeking refuge from debt. He said: Yes, indeed the debtor, when he speaks, lies, and when he promises, breaks his promise."
"4546","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard it from al-Zuhri, by Allah, as I informed you. He said: Urwah narrated to me, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ghusl in the qadah, which is the faraq. She said: I and he used to perform ghusl from a single vessel."
"4547","Sufyan said: And Asim al-Ahwal added, he said: Muadhah narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: So I would say to him: Leave some for me, leave some for me."
"4548","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I memorized from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us every day at both ends of the day. One day he came to us in the midday heat and said: O Abu Bakr, is there any eye upon me? He said: O Messenger of Allah, they are only Umm Ruman, Asma, and Aishah. He said: My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has permitted me to leave. He said: Companionship, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Companionship. Abu Bakr had prepared two mounts, and said: O Messenger of Allah, take one of my two mounts and ride it. He said: No, but for the price, O Abu Bakr."
"4549","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a thief, male or female, and he ordered it, so the hand was cut. And he said: Had it been Fatimah, I would have carried out the hadd upon her."
"4550","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man had a sore or something on his hand, he would say with his finger thus, then say: In the name of Allah, the dust of our land with the saliva of one of us, and our sick is healed by the permission of our Lord."
"4551","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, he heard Abu Bakr ibn Abdurrahman informing from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be overtaken by dawn while in a state of janabah, then he would fast."
"4552","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abu Said narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved none but one of piety."
"4553","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Talhah, from his paternal aunt Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah the Mother of the Believers, she said: A child of the children of the Ansar was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to pray over him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, glad tidings for him; he never encountered evil nor saw it - or did not comprehend it, or do it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, is it other than that?! Allah created Paradise and created people for it, and created it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers. And He created the Fire and created people for it, creating it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers."
"4554","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard it from Abd Rabbih ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Amputation was for a quarter of a dinar and above."
"4555","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: We set out early with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Batha."
"4556","200 - (4556) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a land called Ghadirah and named it Khadirah."
"4557","201 - (4557) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba (pumpkin vessels), hantam (green jars), and muzaffat (pitched vessels)."
"4558","202 - (4558) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: My mother treated me with fattening (foods), wanting to present me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but it did not work for her until I ate fresh dates with cucumber, then I gained weight with the best weight gain."
"4559","203 - (4559) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit."
"4560","204 - (4560) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Ask Allah for everything, even the shoelace, for if Allah does not make it easy, it will not become easy."
"4561","205 - (4561) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked during the expedition of Tabuk about the sutrah of one who prays, and he said: Like the back of a saddle."
"4562","206 - (4562) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Nafi ibn Sulayman narrated to me, that Muhammad ibn Abi Salih informed him, from his father, that he heard Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the muadhdhin is entrusted, so may Allah guide the imams and pardon the muadhdhins."
"4563","207 - (4563) - Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes enter upon us and say to us: Is there anything with you? We would say: No, and he would say: Then I am fasting. She said: And he entered upon us once, and we said to him: Hays (a dish of dates, cheese and butter) was gifted to us, and we hid some of it for you, so he said: Bring it, for I had been fasting. She said: Then he ate."
"4564","208 - (4564) - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night and day will not pass until al-Lat and al-Uzza are worshipped. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I had thought, when Allah said: {He it is who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all religion, even though the polytheists dislike it}, that this was complete. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be of that whatever Allah wills, then Allah will send a pleasant wind, which will take the soul of whoever has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of good, and the others will remain, and they will return to the religion of their forefathers."
"4565","209 - (4565) - Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban informed me, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from Aishah, she said: I missed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night from the bed, so I searched for him with my hand, and my hand fell upon his feet while they were raised and he was prostrating, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in You from You; I cannot enumerate praise for You, You are as You have praised Yourself."
"4566","210 - (4566) - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Shaybah al-Khudri, that he witnessed Urwah narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are three things I swear upon: Allah does not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share, and the shares of Islam are three: fasting, prayer, and charity; Allah does not take charge of a servant and then entrust him to another on the Day of Resurrection, and no man loves a people except that he will come with them on the Day of Resurrection. And the fourth, if I swore upon it I would not fear sinning: Allah does not conceal (the faults of) His servant in this world except that He will conceal him in the Hereafter. Then Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: When you hear the like of this from the like of Urwah, memorize it."
"4567","211 - (4567) - Ishaq said: And Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Masud narrated to me, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"4568","212 - (4568) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Munib, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three (days)."
"4569","213 - (4569) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The siwak is a purification for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord, and in the black seed there is a cure for every disease except al-sam. I said: And what is al-sam? He said: Death."
"4570","214 - (4570) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Salih, he said: Adi ibn Adi sent me to Safiyyah bint Shaybah, asking her about things she used to narrate, from Aishah, she said: Aishah narrated to me that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no divorce, nor emancipation, in ighlaq (compulsion)."
"4571","215 - (4571) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman ibn Hani narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, he said: I said to her: O mother, uncover for me the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his two companions, so she uncovered three graves, low, spread flat with the red gravel of the courtyard; and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) foremost, and Abu Bakr with his head between the shoulders of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar with his head at the feet of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4572","216 - (4572) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: There was no one with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he emigrated from Makkah to Madinah except Abu Bakr, Amir ibn Fuhayrah, and a man from Banu al-Dil, a polytheist, who was their guide."
"4573","217 - (4573) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, he said: Aishah and Umm Salamah were asked: Which deed was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They both said: That which its doer persists upon, even if little."
"4574","218 - (4574) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Khallad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Said Abu Muslim, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, and I feared that something had been commanded concerning me, so he gave me a choice, and I said: Did you mention this to anyone before me? He said: No. I said: Then I have chosen you. And he gave all his wives a choice, and they chose him, and he did not count it as anything."
"4575","219 - (4575) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Makhlad ibn Khufaf, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that produce (kharaj) is by liability (daman)."
"4576","220 - (4576) - Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus al-Halabi narrated to us, from Ibn Mina, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embrace Ali and kiss him, saying: By my father, the unique martyr! By my father, the unique martyr!"
"4577","221 - (4577) - Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: When I wanted to part the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I made the parting from his crown, and let his forelock fall between his shoulders."
"4578","222 - (4578) - Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: When there was revealed: {And leave Me with the deniers, possessors of ease, and respite them a little}, he said: It was only a short while until the battle of Badr occurred."
"4579","223 - (4579) - Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from al-Baqi, and entered upon me and found me suffering a headache in my head, saying: O my head. He said: Rather, by Allah, O Aishah, O my head. Then he said: And what would harm you if you died before me, so I stood over you and shrouded you, then prayed over you and buried you? She said: By Allah, it is as if I see you, if you did that, returning to my house and consummating marriage therein with one of your wives. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled. She said: And his pain overcame him until it became severe while he was in the house of Maymunah, so he called his wives and asked them to permit him to be nursed in my house, so they permitted him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out walking between two men of his family, one of them al-Fadl ibn Abbas, and another man whose feet dragged, with his head bandaged, until he came to my house. Ubayd Allah said: So I narrated this hadith to Abd Allah ibn Abbas. He said: Do you know who the other man was? He said: I said: No. He said: Ali. Then the Messenger of Allah lost consciousness, and his pain intensified, then he recovered, and said: Pour over me seven waterskins from different wells until I go out to the people and entrust them (with instructions). She said: So we seated him in a washbasin belonging to Hafsah bint Umar, and we poured water over him until he began saying with his hand: Enough, enough. Muhammad said: Then he came out, as Ayyub ibn Bashir narrated to me, with his head bandaged, and sat upon the pulpit, and the first thing he spoke was to invoke blessings upon the companions of Uhud, and he invoked blessings upon them abundantly, then said: A servant from among the servants of Allah, Allah gave him a choice between this world and what is with Allah, so he chose what is with Allah. He said: So Abu Bakr understood it and wept, and knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) meant himself. He said: Gently, O Abu Bakr, look at these doors adjoining the mosque and close them, except what belongs to the house of Abu Bakr, for I do not know anyone who was superior to me in companionship than him."
"4580","224 - (4580) - Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Muadhah, from Aishah: that a woman asked Aishah about the continuous fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: Do you act like his act, for he has been forgiven what preceded of his sin and what remained, and his act was supererogatory? Then Aishah said: As for me, by Allah, I never fasted a night at all; indeed Allah said: {Then complete the fast until the night}."
"4581","225 - (4581) - Jafar narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Muadhah, that a woman asked Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast three days of every month? She said: Yes. I said: Which days of the month did he fast? She said: He did not care which days of the month he fasted."
"4582","226 - (4582) - Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wrapped in a hibarah garment, then it was later removed from him. Al-Qasim said: The remnants of that garment are still with us."
"4583","227 - (4583) - Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthmah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Munib, meaning al-Madani, narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for a Muslim to abandon a Muslim for more than three days; if he meets him and greets him three times, each time he does not return it to him, then he bears his sin along with his own sin."
"4584","228 - (4584) - Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah narrated to me, from Aishah, that she said: The last of his speech, a word I heard from him, while he was saying: Rather, the Highest Companion from Paradise. She said: I said: Then, by Allah, he will not choose us, and I knew that which he used to say to us: A prophet of Allah is not taken until he is given a choice."
"4585","229 - (4585) - Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Utbah narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and reclined in my chamber that day when he entered from the mosque, and a man from the family of Abu Bakr entered upon me, in his hand a green siwak. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it while it was in his hand, a look by which I knew he wanted it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like me to give you this siwak? He said: Yes. So I took it and chewed it for him until I softened it, then gave it to him. She said: He cleaned his teeth with it as well as I ever saw him clean with a siwak before. She said: Then he put it down, and I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) growing heavy in my lap. She said: I went to look at his face, and his gaze had become fixed, while he was saying: Rather, the Highest Companion from Paradise. She said: So I said: You were given a choice, and you chose, by the One who sent you with the truth. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"4586","230 - (4586) - Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Abbad, he said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died between my chest and my throat, in my house, where I wronged no one; and out of my foolishness and young age, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while he was in my lap, I placed his head upon a pillow and stood beating my chest with the women and striking my face."
"4587","231 - (4587) - Jafar narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah."
"4588","232 - (4588) - And from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, he said: Aishah said: When the verse of stoning and ten sucklings of an adult was revealed, it was in a sheet under my bed; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, we were occupied with his death, so a tame sheep entered and ate it."
"4589","233 - (4589) - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, that Zayd narrated to him, that Abu Sallam narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Farrukh narrated to him, that Aishah narrated to him, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The son of Adam was created upon three hundred and sixty joints; when he praises Allah, declares Allah's oneness, seeks Allah's forgiveness, praises Allah, removes a thorn from the path of the Muslims, a stone from the path of the Muslims, enjoins good and forbids evil, to the number of those three hundred and sixty joints, he has been moved away from the Fire, and has safeguarded - or protected - himself that day from the Fire."
"4590","234 - (4590) - Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Mujahid, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"4591","235 - (4591) - Abu Ibrahim Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place a pulpit for Hassan ibn Thabit in the mosque, upon which he would stand and recite poetry, defending the Messenger of Allah; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Allah supports Hassan with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends the Messenger of Allah."
"4592","236 - (4592) - Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hakim ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice in prayer for every addition and omission."
"4593","237 - (4593) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from Aishah, she said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and followed him, and he came to al-Baqi, and said: Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people; you are predecessors for us, and we shall join you; O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, nor test us after them."
"4594","238 - (4594) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever introduces into this matter of ours what is not in it, it is rejected."
"4595","239 - (4595) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to sleep while in a state of janabah, he would not sleep until he performed ablution; and when he wanted to eat, he washed his hands, then ate."
"4596","240 - (4596) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter upon us and say: Has anything come to you this morning? We would say: No, and he would say: I am fasting. She said: And he entered upon us one day and said: Is there anything with you? She said: I said: Yes, hays gifted to us. He said: I had begun the morning fasting, then he called for it and tasted it."
"4597","241 - (4597) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh, from al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, she said: Usamah stumbled at the threshold of the door and was cut on his face, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Aishah, remove the harm from him. But I found it distasteful, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began sucking his wound and spitting it out, saying: Had Usamah been a girl, I would have adorned him and clothed him until I married him off."
"4598","242 - (4598) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq, he said: I heard Aishah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The siwak is a purification for the mouth, pleasing to the Lord."
"4599","243 - (4599) - Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Muzarrid, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The womb (kinship) is a branch from the Most Merciful; whoever joins it, He joins him, and whoever severs it, He severs him."
"4600","244 - (4600) - Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown in a dream-vision a girl in a piece of silk; I uncovered her, and she was you. So I said: If it is from Allah, He will carry it out, two or three times. So Aishah said: He married me after the death of Khadijah, and before his departure to Madinah by two or three years, while I was a girl of seven years; when we arrived, women came to me while I was playing on a swing, and they prepared me and adorned me, then brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he consummated marriage with me while I was a girl of nine years."
"4601","245 - (4601) - Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber and the bribed."
"4602","246 - (4602) - Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Razin al-Bakri, he said: A freedwoman of ours called Salma from Bakr ibn Wail narrated to us, that she heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: O Aishah, is there a morsel? So I brought him a loaf and he placed it upon his mouth, and said: O Aishah, has anything of it entered my stomach? Likewise is the kiss of one who fasts; breaking the fast is only from what enters, not from what comes out."
"4603","247 - (4603) - Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rakahs of Fajr and lighten them, until I would say: Did he recite in them the Opening of the Book?"
"4604","248 - (4604) - Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away in my house, on my day, between my chest and my throat; and Allah joined my saliva with his saliva. Aishah said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr entered with a siwak, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was too weak for it, so I took it, then chewed it, then cleaned his teeth with it."
"4605","249 - (4605) - Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the wind had grown strong, his face would change."
"4606","250 - (4606) - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, he mentioned that he heard it from her, that she saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating with his hands raised, saying: O Allah, I am only a human, so do not punish me; whichever man among the Muslims I harm or revile, do not punish me for it."
"4607","251 - (4607) - Abd Allah ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a severe hardship that will occur before the Dajjal. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, where will the Arabs be then? He said: O Aishah, the Arabs that day will be few. I said: What will suffice the believer that day in food? He said: Glorification, declaring oneness, and magnification. I said: Then which wealth that day is best? He said: A servant boy who gives his family water to drink; as for food, there will be no food."
"4608","252 - (4608) - al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Husayn, meaning al-Jufi, narrated to us, from Ibn al-Sammak, from Aidh, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies on this path, in hajj or umrah, and dies therein, will neither be presented (for reckoning) nor held to account, and it will be said: Enter Paradise."
"4609","253 - (4609) - She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah boasts of those who circumambulate."
"4610","254 - (4610) - al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hassan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I sat weeping at the head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to me: What makes you weep? If you wish to join me, let the provision of a rider suffice you from this world, and do not mix with the rich."
"4611","255 - (4611) - Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man reciting talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: And what is Shubrumah? Then he mentioned kinship. So he said: Did you perform hajj for yourself? He said: No. He said: Perform hajj for yourself, then perform hajj for Shubrumah."
"4612","256 - (4612) - Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, my father informed me, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from his grandmother Rumaythah, she said: I stayed the morning with Aishah, and when morning came, she stood and bathed, then entered a room of hers and closed the door without me. So I said: O Mother of the Believers, I stayed the morning with you only for this hour. She said: Then enter. So I entered, and she prayed eight rakahs; I do not know whether their standing was longer, or their bowing, or their prostration. Then she turned to me, struck my thigh, then said: O Rumaythah, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying them, and even if my father were spread out for me (as a threat) for abandoning them, I would not abandon them."
"4613","257 - (4613) - Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, that sweet water was drawn for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the well of al-Suqya, and sometimes he would say: Sweet water was sought for him."
"4614","258 - (4614) - Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Produce is by liability."
"4615","259 - (4615) - Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I love to pray in the House (Kaaba). So he took my hand until he admitted me into al-Hijr, and said: Pray here, for this is from the House, but your people - or his people - shortened it and removed it from the House."
"4616","260 - (4616) - Harun Abu Musa al-Hammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays ibn Muslim al-Jadali, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from Aishah, that a dried meat of gazelle was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram, so he returned it."
"4617","261 - (4617) - Abu Musa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, in the season before the chiefs. Abu Musa Harun al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. Harun said: And I heard Sufyan saying: Al-washiqah is meat that is cooked then dried."
"4618","262 - (4618) - Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: A man entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he brought him near and drew his seat close; when he left from him, she said: O Messenger of Allah, were you not complaining of this one? He said: Yes, but among the most evil of people are those who are honored out of fear of their evil."
"4619","263 - (4619) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose from his bed in part of the night, and I thought he intended one of his wives, so I followed him until he stood at the graves, and said: Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people, and we shall join you. Then he said: O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, nor test us after them. She said: Then he turned and saw me, and said: Woe to her for what she did, if only she could help it."
"4620","264 - (4620) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from Aishah, she said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the night and followed him, and he was at al-Baqi, and I heard him saying: Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people; you are predecessors for us and we shall join you. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, nor test us after them. Then he turned and looked at me, and said: Woe to her for what she did, if only she could help it."
"4621","265 - (4621) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that Sawdah, when she grew old, granted her day to Aishah. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would divide for me my day and her day, and she was the first woman he married."
"4622","266 - (4622) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to bring a woman to her husband, though she had received nothing of her dowry - the hadith."
"4623","267 - (4623) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be brought children, and he would supplicate for them and bless them; so a boy was brought, and he urinated upon him, so he called for water and poured it after it."
"4624","268 - (4624) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the two rakahs before Fajr and lighten them, until I thought he had recited in them nothing except the Opening of the Book, or he had not recited the Opening of the Book."
"4625","269 - (4625) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Aqil Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, from Buhayyah, that she heard a woman asking Aishah about a woman whose menstruation became disordered, so she does not know how to pray. So Aishah said to her: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman whose menstruation became disordered and blood flowed, and she does not know how to pray, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to order her to consider the extent of what she used to menstruate each month once, while her menstruation was regular, so she should sit for that number of nights and days, then abandon prayer in them and estimate them, then bathe at her purity, then wrap herself with a cloth, then pray; for I hope this is from Satan, and that Allah will remove it from her, if Allah wills. She said: So I ordered her to do it, and Allah removed it from her, so order your companion with that."
"4626","270 - (4626) - Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Umar narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from his grandmother, from Aishah, that she said: I was given nine things no woman was given except Maryam bint Imran: Jibril descended with my image in his palm until he commanded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to marry me; and he married me as a virgin and married no virgin besides me; and he passed away with his head in my lap; and I buried him in my house; and the angels surrounded my house; and revelation would descend upon him while he was among his family and they would disperse from him, yet it would descend upon him while I was with him in his blanket; and I am the daughter of his caliph and his truthful one; and my exoneration descended from heaven; and I was created pure and with a pure one; and I was promised forgiveness and noble provision."
"4627","271 - (4627) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, she said: I asked about the wall (al-Hijr), is it from the House? He said: Yes. So I said: Why did they not include it in the House? He said: Your people lacked funds. She said: So I said to him: What is the matter with its door being raised? He said: Your people did that to admit whom they wished; and were it not that your people are recently from Jahiliyyah, and I fear their hearts would reject it, I would consider including al-Hijr in the House, and sticking its door to the ground."
"4628","272 - (4628) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sariy narrated to us, from Salim ibn Hayyan, from Said ibn Mina, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Were it not for your people being recent from Jahiliyyah, I would have stuck it to the ground, added six cubits to the House from al-Hijr, and made for it an eastern door."
"4629","273 - (4629) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, my father informed me, from Aishah, that Umm Habibah and Umm Salamah mentioned a church in Abyssinia they had seen, in which there were images, and they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: Those people, when a righteous man among them died, built a mosque over his grave and depicted those images in it; those are the most evil of creation before Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"4630","274 - (4630) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: When I was awake he would talk to me, and when I was asleep he would lie down - meaning: when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr."
"4631","275 - (4631) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever supplicates against one who wronged him has taken revenge."
"4632","276 - (4632) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, my father informed me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would extend his head to me while he was in retreat in the mosque, and I would comb it while I was menstruating."
"4633","277 - (4633) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she said: He would fast until we would say: He has fasted, and he would break fast until we would say: He has broken fast; and I never saw him fast in any month more than his fasting in Shaban; he would fast all of Shaban, he would fast Shaban except a little."
"4634","278 - (4634) - Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from his father, from Masruq, he said: Aishah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about turning in prayer. So he said: It is a snatching which Satan snatches from the servant's prayer."
"4635","279 - (4635) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, my father informed me, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."
"4636","280 - (4636) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, my father informed me, from Aishah, that Hind bint Utbah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man, and does not give me what suffices me and my child, while I take from him without his knowledge. So he said: Take what suffices you and your child in a reasonable manner."
"4637","281 - (4637) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be overtaken by dawn while in a state of janabah, then he would begin the morning fasting."
"4638","282 - (4638) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, my father informed me, from Aishah, she said: The day of Ashura was a day Quraysh used to fast in Jahiliyyah, and the Messenger of Allah used to fast it; when he came to Madinah he fasted it and commanded its fasting; when the fast of Ramadan was revealed, Ramadan became the obligation, and Ashura was left; whoever wished fasted it, and whoever wished did not fast it."
"4639","283 - (4639) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Hafsah and I were fasting, then food we desired was presented to us, so we ate of it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and Hafsah hastened to him before me - and she was her father's daughter - and said: O Prophet of Allah, we were fasting today, then food we desired was presented to us, so we ate of it. So he said: Make up another day."
"4640","284 - (4640) - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Saib ibn Barakah narrated to us, from his mother, that she circumambulated with Aishah three circuits of seven; each time she completed seven, she sought refuge between the door and al-Hijr until she completed two rakahs for each seven; and with her were women, and they mentioned Hassan ibn Thabit, and attacked him and reviled him. So she said: Do not revile him; there has befallen him what Allah said: For him is a painful punishment. And he had become blind; by Allah, I hope Allah will admit him to Paradise for words he spoke for Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he says to Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith: And my honor..."
"4641","285 - (4641) - Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Imran ibn Hittan, that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave in his house anything containing a cross except that he broke it. He said: Then he narrated to me once, he said: While I was circumambulating the House with the Mother of the Believers, she was noticed, so she said: Give me a garment. So I gave her a garment, and she said: Does it contain a cross? I said: Yes, so she refused to wear it."
"4642","286 - (4642) - Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah. He said: And Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, that Hafs ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Anas narrated to him, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite? He leaves Asr until when it is between the two horns of Satan - or upon the two horns of Satan - he stands and pecks them like the pecking of a rooster; he does not remember Allah in them except little."
"4643","287 - (4643) - al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Lubabah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite every night Tanzil, the prostration (surah), and al-Zumar."
"4644","288 - (4644) - al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Harun al-Awar, from Budayl, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this letter: {Farawhun wa rayhan} (with fathah on ra)."
"4645","289 - (4645) - Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him, from Aishah, that she said: The first that prayer was obligated, in travel and residence, was two rakahs; then it was increased in residence, and left as it was in travel."
"4646","290 - (4646) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from a journey, and I had hung upon my door a curtain in which were winged horses, so he commanded me and I removed it."
"4647","291 - (4647) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid ibn Wardan, from Urwah, from Aishah, that a freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and his wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: Is there anyone here from his relatives? They said: Yes, so he gave them his wealth."
"4648","292 - (4648) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the aqeeqah for a boy: two equivalent sheep, and for a girl: one sheep."
"4649","293 - (4649) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth narrating from Shahr ibn Hawshab, that a man said to Aishah: One of us speaks to himself about something, if he uttered it his Hereafter would be gone, and if it appeared he would be killed. She said: So she said takbir three times, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it, so he said takbir three times, then said: Only the believer is tested with this."
"4650","294 - (4650) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eight rakahs, besides witr."
"4651","295 - (4651) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, that there was with Aishah a woman from Banu Asad; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: Who is this? Aishah said: She is so-and-so, she does not sleep, mentioning her prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is what you are able, for Allah does not tire until you tire. Aishah said: The most beloved religion is that which its doer persists upon."
"4652","296 - (4652) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in three kinds: among us were those who entered ihram for hajj and umrah together, and among us were those who entered ihram for hajj alone, and among us were those who entered ihram for umrah alone. So whoever had entered ihram for hajj and umrah together did not become lawful from anything forbidden to him until he completed the rites of hajj; and whoever had entered ihram for hajj alone did not become lawful from anything forbidden to him until he completed the rites of hajj; and whoever had entered ihram for umrah alone, then circumambulated the House and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, became lawful from what had been forbidden to him until he begins hajj."
"4653","297 - (4653) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that it was said to her: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do among his family? She said: He would sew his garment and mend his sandal, or something like that."
"4654","298 - (4654) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ali, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I travel, shall I fast? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"4655","299 - (4655) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi, from al-Tufayl, the brother of Aishah from her mother, from Aishah, as Uthman knows, that a Jew saw in a dream: What an excellent people is the nation of Muhammad, were it not that they say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. He said: So that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Do not say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills; say: What Allah alone wills."
"4656","300 - (4656) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, if Allah wills, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay Dhuhr in the heat. Abu Yala said: Thus Abd al-Ala narrated to us, with doubt."
"4657","301 - (4657) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: I heard Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, as Abu Yahya supposes, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr with five rakahs, and did not sit except in the last of them; he stood in all of them except the fifth. Ibn Dawud described it."
"4658","302 - (4658) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would send them and remain, and there would come to him what comes to a lawful one before the sacrificial animals reached Makkah."
"4659","303 - (4659) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I twisted the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands, then he sent them and remained, and he did not abandon anything he used to do."
"4660","304 - (4660) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: The family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wild animal; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, it would play and run hard, coming and going; but when it sensed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had entered, it would lie down and not move as long as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the house, fearing to harm him."
"4661","305 - (4661) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Uthaym Abu Zarr al-Hadrami, he said: Uthaym narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani, from his father, from Aishah, she said: It was my night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he slipped away, and I thought he had only slipped away to one of his wives, so I went out jealous; and I found him prostrating like a thrown garment, and I heard him saying: My darkness and my shadow have prostrated to You, and my heart has believed in You; my Lord, this is my hand and what I have earned against myself; O Tremendous One, hoped for every tremendous thing, forgive the tremendous sin. She said: Then he raised his head and said: What brought you out? She said: A suspicion I suspected. He said: Some suspicion is sin; seek Allah's forgiveness. Jibril came to me and commanded me to say these words you heard, so say them in your prostration; for whoever says them will not raise his head until he is forgiven, I think he said: for him."
"4662","306 - (4662) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Misar, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The dawn never found him with me except sleeping. Abu Yala said: Meaning: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4663","307 - (4663) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Said, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim informed me, that Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr informed him, that Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him, he heard Aishah saying: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have been burnt. So he asked him: What is wrong with him? He said: I broke fast in Ramadan. Then he sat, and a great basket called al-araq containing dates was brought. So he said: Where is the burnt one? The man stood, and said: Give it in charity."
"4664","308 - (4664) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth narrating, from a companion of his, from Ata, he said: Aishah said: The plague was mentioned, so I recalled that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A piercing affliction striking my nation from their enemies among the jinn, a swelling like the swelling of camels; whoever remains steadfast upon it is like one guarding the frontier, whoever is struck by it is a martyr, and whoever flees from it is like one fleeing from the battlefield."
"4665","309 - (4665) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his supplication: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire, from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the grave, from the evil of wealth and poverty, from the evil of life and death, and from the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal. O Allah, wash away my sins with snow and hail water, purify my heart of sins as a white garment is purified of filth, and distance me from my sins as You distanced between the west and the east. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, debt, and sin."
"4666","310 - (4666) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth narrating, from Thabit, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me the mat from the mosque. I said: I am menstruating. He said: Menstruation is not in your hand."
"4667","311 - (4667) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abu al-Jawza, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to open prayer with takbir and recitation with {Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds}; and when he raised his head from bowing he would not prostrate until he stood upright; and when he prostrated and raised his head he would not prostrate until he sat upright; and he would say the tashahhud in every two rakahs; and he would forbid the heel of Satan (sitting like Satan), and he would forbid us to spread the left foot over the right foot; and he would end prayer with taslim."
"4668","312 - (4668) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may act with the deeds of the people of Paradise, while it is written in the Book that he is among the people of the Fire; then before his death he changes and acts with the deeds of the people of the Fire, and enters the Fire. And a man may act with the deeds of the people of the Fire, while it is written in the Book that he is among the people of Paradise; then before his death he changes and acts with the deeds of the people of Paradise, and enters Paradise."
"4669","313 - (4669) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umm Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would frequently say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion and Your obedience. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you frequently supplicate with this, do you fear? He said: And what assures me, when the hearts of the servants are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; when He wills to turn the heart of a servant, He turns it."
"4670","314 - (4670) - al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq ibn Asma al-Jarmi al-Basri narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: My baggage contained lightness, and it was upon a swift camel; and the baggage of Safiyyah contained heaviness, and it was upon a heavy slow camel that delayed the caravan. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Transfer the baggage of Aishah onto the camel of Safiyyah, and transfer the baggage of Safiyyah onto the camel of Aishah until the caravan proceeds. Aishah said: When I saw that, I said: O servants of Allah, this Jewess has overcome us regarding the Messenger of Allah. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Abd Allah, your baggage contained lightness, and the baggage of Safiyyah contained heaviness, so it delayed the caravan; so we transferred her baggage onto your camel, and transferred your baggage onto her camel. She said: So I said: Do you claim that you are the Messenger of Allah? She said: Then he smiled. He said: Are you in doubt, O Umm Abd Allah? She said: I said: Do you claim that you are the Messenger of Allah? Why did you not act justly? And Abu Bakr heard me, and he had sharpness, that is harshness, so he came upon me and slapped my face. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Abu Bakr. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what she said? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The jealous one does not see the bottom of the valley from its top."
"4671","315 - (4671) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu Atiyyah, from Aishah, she said: I know how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite talbiyah; she would recite talbiyah: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours."
"4672","316 - (4672) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Rabiah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Ibn Judan used to feed the guest, be good to the neighbor, join kinship, and withhold harm; will that benefit him anything? He said: No, O Aishah, he never said a single day: My Lord, forgive me on the Day of Judgment."
"4673","317 - (4673) - Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while she was a girl of six years, and consummated marriage with her while she was a girl of nine years; Abu Bakr married her to him."
"4674","318 - (4674) - Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, that Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while he was sixty-three years old. He said: And Ibn al-Musayyib informed me of that."
"4675","319 - (4675) - Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed me, that Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to him, that Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to him, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man recited this verse: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it}. So he said: Shall we be recompensed for all we did? Then we are ruined. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Yes, the believer is recompensed for it in this world, in affliction in his body, in what harms him."
"4676","320 - (4676) - Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Ghalib, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a life for a life, the married adulterer, and the one who abandons his religion."
"4677","321 - (4677) - Abu Mamar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, he said: Abu Hurayrah sat at the chamber of Aishah while she was praying, narrating, saying: Do you not hear, O mistress of the chamber? When she completed her prayer, she said: O Urwah, do you not listen to this one and to his hadith? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate a narration such that if a counter counted it, he could enumerate it."
"4678","322 - (4678) - Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abu Sufyan al-Mamari narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the doors to be closed, except the door of Abu Bakr, or the small door of Abu Bakr. He said: And Aishah said: I did not know my parents except that they professed this religion."
"4679","323 - (4679) - Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Rifaa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring near to us the blessed morning meal, meaning: sahur; and sometimes there was nothing but two dates. Al-Zuhri said: Sahur is sunnah."
"4680","324 - (4680) - And from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who removes her clothes in other than the house of her husband has torn every veil between her and Allah."
"4681","325 - (4681) - Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said: I heard Aishah weeping. So I said: O Mother of the Believers, what makes you weep? She said: I ate to fullness today, and recalled that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate to fullness twice in a day."
"4682","326 - (4682) - Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Zamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid."
"4683","327 - (4683) - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Hamdani narrated to us, Khallad al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she used to carry Zamzam water in bottles, and she mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to carry it."
"4684","328 - (4684) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Hafs ibn Bishr al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice for every addition and omission."
"4685","329 - (4685) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Said ibn Shurahbil narrated to us, from Layth ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Ibn Abbas, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people, saying: Your place from Paradise - meaning: whoever guards what is between his jaws and guards what is between his legs."
"4686","330 - (4686) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for one of his wives with two mudds of barley."
"4687","331 - (4687) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would rise for ablution, he would tilt the vessel, mention Allah's name, then perform ablution thoroughly."
"4688","332 - (4688) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Rushdayn ibn Sad, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dying, with a cup containing water beside him; he would put his hand in and wipe his face, then say: O Allah, help me with the agonies of death."
"4689","333 - (4689) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Imran ibn Anas, Abu Anas al-Makki, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Do you know what is the greatest adultery before Allah? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The greatest adultery before Allah is deeming the honor of a Muslim man lawful, then he recited: {And those who harm the believing men and believing women for other than what they earned}."
"4690","334 - (4690) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, grant me health in my body, grant me health in my sight, and make it the inheritor from me; there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Tremendous Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"4691","335 - (4691) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Israil, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Jabir al-Allaf, Ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere."
"4692","336 - (4692) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4693","336 - (4692) - (M) - And from Hajjaj, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, they both said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. And in the hadith of Urwah: And the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"4694","337 - (4693) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Sayfi ibn Ribi al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a swallowing (of the earth), transformation, and pelting, that will occur at the end of this nation. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while among us are the righteous? He said: Yes, when wickedness appears."
"4695","338 - (4694) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who sees in a dream that he had a wet dream, but sees no wetness. He said: No washing upon him. Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, and a woman who sees that? He said: Women are the counterparts of men."
"4696","339 - (4695) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abd Allah Abu al-Muhajir, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abu Hurayrah and Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times."
"4697","340 - (4696) - Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan saying: I said to Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim: Did you hear your father informing from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting? He said: He was silent toward me for a while, then said to me: Yes, as if he deemed me young."
"4698","341 - (4697) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had intercourse with her without ejaculation. She said: So we both bathed."
"4699","342 - (4698) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded building mosques in neighborhoods, that they be cleaned and perfumed."
"4700","343 - (4699) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from his father, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from al-Bahiyy, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to remember Allah in all his states."
"4701","Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar who said: Aishah said: I never saw anyone at all more truthful than Fatimah except her father, and there was something between them, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, ask her, for she does not lie."
"4702","Ahmad ibn Janab narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah who said: My brother Abdullah ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, who said: Eleven women gathered and pledged and agreed not to conceal anything of their husbands' affairs. The first said: My husband is like lean camel meat on a mountain top, neither easy to climb nor fat to carry off. The second said: I will not spread my husband's news, for I fear I may not leave him; if I mention him I mention his defects and blemishes. The third said: My husband is the tall lout; if I stay silent I am left suspended, and if I speak I am divorced. The fourth said: My husband is like the night of Tihamah, neither hot nor cold, neither fear nor boredom. The fifth said: My husband, when he eats he wraps up, when he drinks he sips up, when he sleeps he wraps himself, and he does not insert his hand to know my grief. The sixth said: My husband is dim-witted or helpless - Isa doubted - a blight, every disease has a disease; he may wound your head or break you or gather all to you. The seventh said: My husband, when he enters he is like a lion, when he goes out he is like a leopard, and he does not ask about what he left behind. The eighth said: My husband, his touch is like a rabbit's touch and his scent like the scent of zarnab. The ninth said: My husband is lofty in pillar, long in sword-belt, great in ashes, his house near the gathering place. The tenth said: My husband is Malik, and what is Malik, better than that; he has camels few in pasture but many at the resting place; when they hear the lute they know they are to be slaughtered. The eleventh said: My husband is Abu Zar, and what is Abu Zar; he loaded my ears with jewelry and filled my arms with fat, and he honored me so I honored myself, and he found me among a small flock of sheep in hardship and made me among horses and camels and threshing floors and winnowers. With him I speak and am not rebuked, I sleep and sleep till morning, I drink and drink my fill. The mother of Abu Zar, and what is the mother of Abu Zar? Her provision vessels are full and her house spacious. The son of Abu Zar, and what is the son of Abu Zar? His bed is like a stripped sword blade, and the forearm of a young goat satisfies him. The daughter of Abu Zar, and what is the daughter of Abu Zar? Obedient to her father and mother, full in her cloak, and the anger of her co-wife. The maid of Abu Zar, and what is the maid of Abu Zar? She does not spread our talk, nor carry off our food, nor fill our house with rubbish. Abu Zar went out while the milk-skins were being churned, and met a woman with two sons like leopards playing with two pomegranates under her waist, so he divorced me and married her, then I married after him a noble man who rode a swift horse and took a spear and brought me abundant cattle. He said: Eat, Umm Zar, and provide for your family. She said: If I gathered all he gave me it would not reach the smallest vessel of Abu Zar. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Aish, I am to you like Abu Zar to Umm Zar."
"4703","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rayhan ibn Said al-Naji narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, with the hadith of Umm Zar, nearly the same."
"4704","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Shabur, from Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah, from his grandfather Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that she narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Abu Zar and Umm Zar, and she mentioned the poetry of Abu Zar about Umm Zar."
"4705","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created the heavens? He says: Allah. Then he says: Who created the earth? He says: Allah. Then he says: Who created Allah? So when that happens, let him say: I believe in Allah and His messengers."
"4706","Ahmad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Aflah ibn Humayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of his wives, then he slept until morning while junub, then he bathed and fasted his day."
"4707","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ishaq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ata, that Masruq asked Aishah, saying: O my mother, if a man wakes junub, does he fast that day? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke junub from intercourse, not a wet dream, for an obligatory fast not a voluntary one, then he bathed and prayed and completed his fast."
"4708","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake while junub and complete his fast."
"4709","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to the Fajr prayer with his head dripping from intercourse, not a wet dream, then he would fast."
"4710","Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend the night, then Bilal would call him with the adhan, so he would rise and bathe, and I would see water running down his skin and hair, then he would go out and pray and I would hear his weeping, then he would remain fasting. He said: I said to al-Shabi: In Ramadan? He said: The same."
"4711","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah who said: We wrote to Ibrahim ibn Yazid asking him about suckling, and he wrote that Shurayh narrated that Ali and Ibn Masud used to say: Little and much of suckling makes unlawful. He said: And in his letter was that Abu al-Shatha al-Muharibi narrated that Aishah narrated that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: One or two snatches do not make unlawful."
"4712","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, that when Rafi ibn Khadij died, Abdullah ibn Umar said: Do not weep over him, for the weeping of the living over the dead is punishment upon the dead. So Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said it about a Jewess whose family were weeping over her: They are weeping over her while she is punished in her grave."
"4713","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that he heard Aishah, and she spread her hands, saying: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two hands of mine for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his release before he circumambulated the House."
"4714","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a cloud he was alarmed by it and his color changed, and he came forward and went back and entered and went out, then when it rained he was relieved. Aishah said: I asked him about that, and he said: How do you know, perhaps it is as He said: Then when they saw it as a cloud approaching their valleys they said: This is a cloud bringing us rain, the verse."
"4715","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: I said to Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim: Did you hear your father reporting from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her while fasting? He said: Yes."
"4716","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"4717","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss in the month of fasting."
"4718","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, that she said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I see jihad as the best deed, shall we not fight? He said: But the best jihad is an accepted pilgrimage."
"4719","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad who said: I asked Aishah about touching for one fasting and she disliked it, so I said to her: I heard that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch while fasting? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had most control of his desire of all people."
"4720","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father who said: Aishah said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeing nothing but Hajj, then when we were at Sarif or near it I menstruated, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me while I was weeping. He said: What is wrong, have you menstruated? I said: Yes. He said: This is a matter Allah decreed for the daughters of Adam, so perform what the pilgrim performs except do not circumambulate the House until you bathe. Then when we were at Mina the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed cows on behalf of his wives."
"4721","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl who said: They used to like that when a man finished prayer he say: O Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace, blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"4722","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say these words."
"4723","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray any of the night prayer sitting, until when he advanced in age he prayed and recited, then when thirty or forty verses of the surah remained he stood and recited, then bowed."
"4724","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me from a journey, and I had screened a recess of mine with a curtain in which were images. When he saw it he tore it down with his hand and said: The most severely punished people before Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate Allah's creation. Aishah said: So we cut it and made from it one or two cushions."
"4725","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Umm Musa who said: I saw Ali ibn Abi Talib praying after Asr."
"4726","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Umm Musa, who said: Najiyah bint Qarazah sent me to Aishah to ask her about prayer after Asr. She said: I went to her, not caring what she said after what I had seen of Ali. She said: She reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray after Asr."
"4727","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe, scooping from it while we were junub."
"4728","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from his mother, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating, then recite the Quran."
"4729","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray standing and sitting; when he prayed standing he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting he bowed sitting."
"4730","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep junub as he was, not touching water."
"4731","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I said to her: I do not care, O mother, if I do not walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah. She said: What an evil thing you said, O son of my sister; those who entered ihram for Manat at al-Mushallal would not walk between them - or circumambulate between them, Sufyan doubted - so Allah revealed: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah, the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked between them, so it is a sunnah."
"4732","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Furat ibn Salman, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing Islam is overturned like a vessel is overturned in a drink called tila."
"4733","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Said Abu Masud al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq who said: I said to Aishah: O Mother of the Believers, which of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was dearest to him? She said: Abu Bakr. I said: Then whom? She said: Then Umar. He said: I said: Then whom? She said: Then Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. He said: I said: Then whom? He said: Then she fell silent."
"4734","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from his mother, from Aishah, that a woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about her washing from menstruation, and he told her how to wash, then said: Take a piece of musk and purify yourself with it. She said: How do I purify myself with it? She said: He covered his face with the edge of his garment and said: Glory be to Allah, purify yourself with it. Aishah said: So I pulled the woman and said: Follow the trace of blood with it."
"4735","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss some of his wives while fasting, then she laughed."
"4736","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shimr ibn Atiyah, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Aishah: That she rode a camel and cursed it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not ride it."
"4737","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Said ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from Abu Talhah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not enter a house in which is a dog or images. He said: I said: Let us go to Aishah, so we told her what Abu Talhah said, and she said: I do not know, but I will tell you what I saw him do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on one of his expeditions, and I awaited his return, so I took a rug of ours and screened the عرض with it. She said: When he came I stood and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, praise be to Allah who strengthened you and aided you and honored you. She said: He raised his head and looked at the rug and did not return anything to me; I recognized dislike in his face, so he went until he tore the rug, then said: O Aishah, Allah did not command us in what He provided us to clothe stones and bricks. She said: So I took it and made it a cushion, then stuffed it with fiber, and he did not object to that."
"4738","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray nine rakahs at night."
"4739","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah preferred the prayer for which he uses the siwak over the prayer for which he does not use it seventyfold. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preferred the hidden remembrance which the guardian angels do not hear seventyfold, saying: When the Day of Resurrection comes and Allah gathers mankind for their reckoning, and the guardians come with what they kept and wrote, Allah says to them: See, is anything left for him? They say: Our Lord, we left nothing of what we knew and kept except we counted and wrote it. Then Allah, blessed and exalted, says to him: You have with Me a treasure you do not know, and I will reward you for it, and it is the hidden remembrance."
"4740","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya al-Sadafi, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying in my house, then Ali ibn Abi Talib came and stood beside him on his right, then a scorpion came toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when it drew near him it was turned away from him, then it came toward Ali, so he took the sandal and killed it while praying. When he finished his prayer he said: May Allah destroy it; it came toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then was turned from him, then came to me intending me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw no harm in killing it during prayer."
"4741","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah reported to me, from Aishah who said: By Allah, I argued back with the Messenger of Allah, and nothing made me argue so much except that it never occurred to me that people would ever love a man who stood in his place."
"4742","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, my father reported to me, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love sweets and honey."
"4743","Abu Said narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah who said: A gift was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was fasting, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, were it not for your fasting we would have given you something. He said: Bring it."
"4744","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek breakfast, and we would say: There is nothing, so he would say: I am fasting."
"4745","Abu Said narrated to us, Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from the end of his day after praying Zuhr, then returned and stayed at Mina the nights of the days of Tashriq, stoning the jamrah when the sun declined, each jamrah seven pebbles, standing at the first and the second, prolonging the standing and supplicating humbly, then stoning the third jamrah and not standing at it."
"4746","Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, Umar ibn Saad al-Nasri narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the rulers, woe to the headmen, woe to the trustees; there will come upon one of them a day when he wishes he were suspended by a star and had never been in charge of anything."
"4747","Ismail ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to set a pulpit for Hassan in the mosque, on which he would stand defending or boasting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Allah supports Hassan with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends - or boasts - for the Messenger of Allah."
"4748","Ismail ibn Musa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out to these watercourses."
"4749","Ismail ibn Musa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from Aishah who said: I missed him at night - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and there he was at al-Baqi. He said: Peace be upon you, abode of believing people; you are predecessors for us and we shall join you; O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward nor tempt us after them."
"4750","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"4751","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Sulayman ibn Musa reported to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married except with her guardian's permission; if she is married, her marriage is void, and if he consummated with her, she gets her dowry for what he took from her, and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"4752","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Rabiah al-Jurashi, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Shaban and Ramadan, and would seek to fast Mondays and Thursdays."
"4753","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Dawud reported to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Ata, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with one rakah."
"4754","Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Ghibtah Umm Amr al-Mujashiiyah narrated to me, saying: My aunt narrated to me, from my grandmother, from Aishah who said: I asked her about the woman who joins hair, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the one who asks for it."
"4755","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ghibtah Umm Amr, an old woman of Banu Mujashi, narrated to me, my aunt narrated to me, from my grandmother, from Aishah who said: Hind bint Utbah ibn Rabiah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him, and he looked at her hands and said to her: Go and change your hands. She said: So she went and changed them with henna, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I pledge you on that you associate nothing with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery. She said: Does a free woman commit adultery? He said: Nor kill your children fearing poverty. She said: Did you leave us any children to kill? She said: So she pledged him, then said to him, wearing two gold bracelets: What do you say about these two bracelets? He said: Two coals of the coals of Hell."
"4756","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Murrah al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Isl ibn Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not chant the Quran is not of us."
"4757","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah: That she wanted to free two slaves of hers who were a married couple, and she mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Begin with the man."
"4758","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, saying: I heard Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman say: I heard Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman narrating from Aishah that she said: I found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a writing: The most insolent people are one who strikes one who did not strike him, and a man who kills one other than his killer, and a man who takes as master other than his benefactors; whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His messenger, Allah accepts from him neither exchange nor ransom. And in requital: The blood of the believers is equal, and the least of them grants protection. No Muslim is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant during his covenant, nor do people of two religions inherit from one another, nor is a woman married together with her paternal aunt nor her maternal aunt, nor any prayer after Asr until the sun sets, nor does a woman travel three nights with other than a mahram."
"4759","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abi Namir reported to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Aishah, that she said: Whenever it was her night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out at the end of the night to al-Baqi and say: Peace be upon you, abode of believing people; what you were promised has come to you, deferred till tomorrow, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you; O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi al-Gharqad."
"4760","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Khayrah bint Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Siba, from her mother, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek good with the handsome of face."
"4761","Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttuli narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about poetry, and he said: It is speech; its good is good and its ugly is ugly."
"4762","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies owing fasts, his guardian fasts on his behalf."
"4763","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab at Mina saying: O people, departure is tomorrow, so let none depart until he circumambulates the House, for the last rite is circumambulation."
"4764","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah and Abdullah ibn Amir reported to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, and from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same, except he said: Then let her depart."
"4765","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abu Lubabah narrated to us, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite every night Tanzeel, the prostration surah, and al-Zumar."
"4766","Al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Water, nothing makes it impure."
"4767","Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Saad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two rakahs of Fajr are better than the world and what is in it."
"4768","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim Abu Abdullah al-Nukri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, the blood of a Muslim man who testifies there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful."
"4769","Al-Amash said: I narrated it to Ibrahim, and he narrated to me from al-Aswad, from Aishah, similarly."
"4770","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The kidney vein, which is the flank, would seize the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a month, so he could not go out to the people, and I saw him in pain so I would take his hand and spit in it with the Quran, then pour it over his face, seeking thereby the blessing of the Quran and the blessing of his hand. I would say: O Messenger of Allah, your supplication is answered, so pray to Allah to relieve you of what you are in. He would say: O Aishah, I am the most severely tried of people."
"4771","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ayyub ibn Bashir, from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness: Pour over me seven skins of water from seven different wells. So they did."
"4772","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani, from Aishah who said: A vessel would be brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I would take it and place my lips on it, then he would take it and place his lips on the place of my lips; and I would take the bone and bite from it, then he would place his mouth on the place of my mouth, while I was menstruating."
"4773","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed and wanted to sleep while junub before bathing, he performed ablution fully, then slept."
"4774","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I do not accept a gift from a Bedouin. Then Umm Sunbulah al-Aslamiyyah came to him with a skin of milk as a gift to him. He said: Pour from it into this cup. So she poured, and he took it and drank. I said: Did you not say: I do not accept a gift from a Bedouin? He said: The Bedouins of Aslam are not Bedouins, but they are our desert folk and we are their townsfolk; if we call them they answer us, and if they call us we answer them."
"4775","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, al-Sari ibn Ismail narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would order his bed, and it would be spread for him, and he would face the qiblah. When he lay on it he pillowed his right hand, then whispered, we did not know what he said, then at the end of that he raised his voice and said: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, God - or Lord - of everything, Revealer of the Torah and the Gospel and the Criterion, Splitter of grain and seed, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock You hold. O Allah, You are the First, there is nothing before You, and the Last, there is nothing after You, and You are the Manifest, there is nothing above You, and You are the Hidden, there is nothing beneath You; settle our debt and free us from poverty."
"4776","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab narrated to us, from Talhah, freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died with an empty belly."
"4777","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, that Saibah reported to him that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing snakes except the short-tailed and the one with two stripes, for they snatch sight and cause what is in women's wombs to miscarry; whoever leaves them is not of us."
"4778","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me and there came over him from Allah what used to come over him, so he was covered with his garment and a leather cushion was placed under his head, then he sat with what looked like pearls streaming from him, while he wiped it off."
"4779","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: When revelation descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he felt what Allah Almighty said: Indeed We shall cast upon you a heavy word."
"4780","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Humayd, from Abu al-Malih who said: Abdullah ibn Rabah al-Ansari narrated to us, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rakahs before dawn, then say in his prayer place: O Allah, Lord of Gabriel and Michael, Lord of Israfil and Lord of Muhammad, I seek refuge in You from the Fire, then go out to his prayer."
"4781","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Tamim, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Aishah said: Blessed is He whose hearing encompasses everything; I hear the speech of Khawlah bint Thalabah while some of it escapes me, as she complains of her husband to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, he consumed my youth and I bore children for him, until when my age grew and my childbearing ended, he declared zihar on me. O Allah, I complain to You. She said: She had not left before Gabriel came down with these verses: Allah has heard the speech of the woman who disputes with you about her husband and complains to Allah."
"4782","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham, from Salih ibn Rabiah ibn Hudayr, from Aishah who said: Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was with him, so I stood and shut the door between me and him. When it was lifted from him he said: O Aishah, Gabriel sends you greetings of peace."
"4783","Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yunus reported it to me, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wanted to sleep while junub would perform his ablution for prayer, then when he wanted to eat he washed his hands, then ate."
"4784","Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yunus reported to me, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No fulfilling a vow in disobedience to Allah, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"4785","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala al-Taifi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never slept before Isha nor stayed up after it."
"4786","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Aflah ibn Humayd reported to me, that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrating, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with his wife and did not bathe until morning, then bathed and prayed and fasted that day."
"4787","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Salamah narrated to me, Aishah narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two light rakahs between the call and the iqamah."
"4788","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to me, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, Aishah narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray between the last Isha prayer until dawn breaks eleven rakahs, giving salam between every two, praying witr with one, and staying in his prostration as long as one of you recites fifty verses. When the first caller for Fajr prayer fell silent, he stood and bowed two light rakahs, then lay on his right side until the caller came to him."
"4789","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night in Ramadan to the mosque after Isha and prayed, and people saw him and prayed with his prayer. The next night he went out too, and people saw him and gathered and magnified Allah and prayed with his prayer. On the third night the mosque was full, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go out to them, and they acted as if calling him to come out to them. He said: O Aishah, what is wrong with the people? I said: O Messenger of Allah, they prayed with you these two nights and loved that you come out to them. Then he went out to them and said: O people, upon you are deeds you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire, and the most beloved deeds to Allah are the most constant though little. You persisted until I feared it would be prescribed upon you. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven standing and two sitting; when he wanted to bow he stood and recited, then bowed, then prayed witr with one. Abu Salamah said: I said: How was his prayer in Ramadan? She said: He would not exceed this in Ramadan."
"4790","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk and gold, drinking in silver vessels, and red saddle cloths. Aishah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a thin thing of gold with which the المسك is tied? He said: Make it silver and yellow it with some saffron."
"4791","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah who said: Whoever tells you the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urinate standing, disbelieve him; I saw him urinating sitting."
"4792","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim said: Musa ibn Ayan al-Harrani narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray nine rakahs at night."
"4793","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid al-Himsi Abu Yuhmid narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Zubaydi, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sometimes applied kohl while fasting."
"4794","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray nine rakahs of the night."
"4795","Al-Mualla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad who said: I asked Aishah about the night prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: He would sleep the first of the night and rise at its end, praying what was decreed for him. When he finished his prayer he inclined to his bed; if he had need of his family he went to his family, then slept as he was without touching water. When he heard the first adhan - or the caller - he rose; if junub he bathed, and if not junub he performed his ablution for prayer, then prayed two rakahs, then went out to the mosque."
"4796","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Abdullah ibn Maqil, from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed standing he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting he bowed sitting."
"4797","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose for ablution he overturned the vessel, mentioned Allah's name, then performed ablution fully."
"4798","Zakariya ibn Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Said al-Raqashi, a Basran, narrated to us, Ibn Hilal Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in prayer over the dead: O Allah, forgive him, bless him, favor him, and bring him to the pond of Your messenger."
"4799","Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Raqashi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Musa al-Makki narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Aishah bint Saad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let Abu Bakr pray with the people. They said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you ordered another to pray? He said: It is not fitting for my nation that an imam lead them while Abu Bakr is among them."
"4800","Zakariya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Waki, Abdullah ibn Dawud, Uththam ibn Ali, and Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman with prolonged bleeding prays, even if blood drips on the mat. Ibn Dawud said: Drop by drop."
